{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age","id":1409323,"title":"What do you guys think of Dreams of the First Age?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-08-20T04:01:49-07:00","id":1409323,"title":"What do you guys think of Dreams of the First Age?","content":"It\u2019s the first thing I ever read for Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-20T04:46:24-07:00","id":1409327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age#post1409323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s the first thing I ever read for Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Dreams box set epitomized Exalted 2nd Edition, for better or worse. One's opinion on Dreams is inseparable from one's opinion on 2E.<br /> <br /> I loved Dreams. It felt like vindication for every rebuffed claim I ever made during 1E. It was the natural successor to Wonders of the Lost Age which (admittedly unintentionally) had set the tone for 2E.<br /> <br /> Dreams was to Exalted as Warhammer 30k was to Warhammer 40k. (Or as 40k was to Warhammer.)<br /> <br /> Dreams was Pathfinder 1 to 3.5.<br /> <br /> Dreams was Vanilla Coke.<br /> <br /> Dreams was <i>Chocolate</i> Milk.<br /> <br /> If you hated how 2E robbed away all the mystery of 1E, you must have <i>loathed</i> Dreams. But if you delved into every scrap of lore, every hint, every background picture to obsessively piece together Exalted's secret history then Dreams was the Holy Grail of sourcebooks.<br /> <br /> People joke about Exalted being &quot;Rapters in an F-16&quot;, but Dreams really was Rapters in an F-16. Power Armored police detaining a suspect's ghost! ApplePay made of hardened magic! It was a realistic, down to Earth game that was completely off the wall and filled with magic robots.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong. I like 3E. 3E is far more playable than 2E ever was. I could never &quot;go back&quot;. And I understand that lots of people hated it.<br /> <br /> But I loved Dreams.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-20T05:01:54-07:00","id":1409328,"title":"","content":"Dreams of the First Age was both wonderful and terrible. You got genuine glimpses of the way a society with Exalted could have been like at its height... you also got a lot of very bad and lazy writing. I don't just mean the charms and mechanics, although those were absolutely terrible in execution; Dreams is what we have to thank for the &quot;Every Lunar is abused by their Solar spouse like this was an old Jerry Springer show&quot;, the &quot;Dragon-blooded are trash who are barely above mortals&quot;, and similar things that were ultimately harmful to the line, in my opinion.<br /> <br /> But on the <i>other</i> hand, there's a lot of other things I thought were great. Manuals for military commanders to handle one of their soldiers suddenly Exalting (and the Exalted generally not oppressing mortal humans as much as you might think because the next of their number could come from there - although of course there were exceptions), Hell being considered so utterly subjugated that the Deliberative offered members tours through it as a tourist attraction...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-20T06:32:43-07:00","id":1409338,"title":"","content":"I wanted to like Dreams but ultimately consider Glories of the Most High to be a much better First Age supplement.<br /> <br /> By reintroducing the Celestial Incarna as stated NPCs to be interact with rather than setting decoration it made the setting larger and more mythical. The charms in Glories, especially the Solar Charms are First Age charms and tell a story of their excess (accessing Abyssal charms, abusing the Solar Bond etc) while the ones in DotFA were just high essence.<br /> <br /> Now Zeal arguably said <i>something</i>, but if it did then that tone wasn't carried forth into the rest of the supplement.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-20T06:40:21-07:00","id":1409340,"title":"","content":"We don't talk about Zeal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-20T06:58:07-07:00","id":1409342,"title":"","content":"You got me curious. What is Zeal ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-20T07:10:35-07:00","id":1409345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1409342#post1409342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You got me curious. What is Zeal ?</div> </div> </div> </div>A broken charm.<br /> <br /> Like, not broken in the sense of being non-balanced, but broken like a couple of other 2nd edition charms as originally printed in that it <i>literally did not work</i>. It attempted to be a 'transperfect' charm, i.e., an attack that could break through a perfect defense charm. Except what balance 2e combat had was <i>entirely predicated</i> on &quot;defense always wins ties&quot;. If I have a &quot;I will always hit you no matter what&quot; charm, and you have a &quot;I parry absolutely everything, no matter what&quot; charm, <i>your charm always wins, as described in the 2e corebook.</i><br /> <br /> Which meant either Zeal did literally nothing, or it actually broke what little balance the combat system possessed since now any kind of attack from ambush was guaranteed to vaporize whatever it hit, from a sufficently powerful Solar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-20T07:28:00-07:00","id":1409347,"title":"","content":"Nitpick.<br /> <br /> Zeal still did something and was still broken even if the core rules didn't allow it to function as a transperfect attack as the author intended, because even without that aspect of the charm it was still an underpriced perfect effect that could be used with any ability provided the action aligned with a Virtue.<br /> <br /> It's loathsome to me for the same reason Void Avatar Prana was, because a lot of people identified it right away and went &quot;as long as we don't use that, the rest of the book is basically fine...&quot; in both cases that was very wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 08-20-2020, 10:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-20T08:22:31-07:00","id":1409357,"title":"","content":"Sidereal Martial Arts too, for that matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-20T08:24:20-07:00","id":1409358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aliasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1409345#post1409345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A broken charm.<br /> <br /> Like, not broken in the sense of being non-balanced, but broken like a couple of other 2nd edition charms as originally printed in that it <i>literally did not work</i>. It attempted to be a 'transperfect' charm, i.e., an attack that could break through a perfect defense charm. Except what balance 2e combat had was <i>entirely predicated</i> on &quot;defense always wins ties&quot;. If I have a &quot;I will always hit you no matter what&quot; charm, and you have a &quot;I parry absolutely everything, no matter what&quot; charm, <i>your charm always wins, as described in the 2e corebook.</i><br /> <br /> Which meant either Zeal did literally nothing, or it actually broke what little balance the combat system possessed since now any kind of attack from ambush was guaranteed to vaporize whatever it hit, from a sufficently powerful Solar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems interesting. I'd like they don't do that in 3e. Also, does transperfect exist ? All I can find is a company and some LinkedIn stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-20T09:02:32-07:00","id":1409363,"title":"","content":"The errata charms for dreams helped a lot, as someone fond of elder play I was very happy with it. It also gave us the only hard numbers for what an allies 3 or mentor 4 meant with an exalt. From a fluff perspective I enjoyed it a lot, seeing the interconnections to the age of sorrows locations, ancient wonders and cities repurposed, and also just fun stuff like the immaculate order being a postal service originally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1166-korekore","name":"korekore","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1166_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-20T09:10:40-07:00","id":1409368,"title":"","content":"I really like DotFA, except for the part about Lilith being abused. I also liked Glories of the Most High. I never actually played Exalted or read the 2e corebook (did read 3e), so idk which is better overall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-20T10:04:56-07:00","id":1409376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1409358#post1409358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, does transperfect exist ? </div> </div> </div> </div>She means transcendantly perfect. An effect which is better than the perfect effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-20T10:12:32-07:00","id":1409377,"title":"","content":"I think that Dreams of the First Age is a fine option for what the first age looked like. I blanch at it being the only option, the canon option, or that there even is a canon first age.<br /> <br /> IMO The first age should be fairly nebulous so that, if the specifics of it matter at all, they can be specifics set by a storyteller to reinforce the themes and plot points of the story the group is telling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-20T10:43:31-07:00","id":1409380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aliasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1409328#post1409328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dreams of the First Age was both wonderful and terrible. You got genuine glimpses of the way a society with Exalted could have been like at its height... you also got a lot of very bad and lazy writing. I don't just mean the charms and mechanics, although those were absolutely terrible in execution; Dreams is what we have to thank for the &quot;Every Lunar is abused by their Solar spouse like this was an old Jerry Springer show&quot;, the &quot;Dragon-blooded are trash who are barely above mortals&quot;, and similar things that were ultimately harmful to the line, in my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure those bits of toxic memetic fluff were doing their tasteless job a bunch of books before DotFA, harkening to at least CoCD1 in the case of the Dragon-Blooded, probably even before in the case of Lilith &amp; Desus. In fact, ain't Desus gone from canon in 3e? If so, honestly good riddance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1409338#post1409338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wanted to like Dreams but ultimately consider Glories of the Most High to be a much better First Age supplement.<br /> <br /> By reintroducing the Celestial Incarna as stated NPCs to be interact with rather than setting decoration it made the setting larger and more mythical. The charms in Glories, especially the Solar Charms are First Age charms and tell a story of their excess (accessing Abyssal charms, abusing the Solar Bond etc) while the ones in DotFA were just high essence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed, on oh-so many levels - the accessing Abyssal charms one i used as springboard for a major &quot;Deathlord but not&quot; npc i would introduce in my games, among other things. And i mine Glories for inspiration to this day even while making no appearance of the Incarna whatsoever. It's a great book indeed that delivers the mythic in a manner that only Scion comes close to in its own way i guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 08-20-2020, 01:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-20T10:54:18-07:00","id":1409383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1409347#post1409347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nitpick.<br /> <br /> Zeal still did something and was still broken even if the core rules didn't allow it to function as a transperfect attack as the author intended, because even without that aspect of the charm it was still an underpriced perfect effect that could be used with any ability provided the action aligned with a Virtue.<br /> <br /> It's loathsome to me for the same reason Void Avatar Prana was, because a lot of people identified it right away and went &quot;as long as we don't use that, the rest of the book is basically fine...&quot; in both cases that was very wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fun bit on Zeal, is that author I think also wrote the attempts of transperfects in <b>Scroll of the Monk</b> as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-20T10:54:30-07:00","id":1409384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1409368#post1409368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really like DotFA, except for the part about Lilith being abused. I also liked Glories of the Most High. I never actually played Exalted or read the 2e corebook (did read 3e), so idk which is better overall.</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of my antipathy towards Dreams of the First Age has come from actually trying to engage it as a playable setting and realising that despite having two books worth of content it's badly lacking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-20T11:07:12-07:00","id":1409389,"title":"","content":"On Dreams, I think I found it fine at the time, but mostly since I like Neph and think what he wrote was at least interesting. As a book though I think it kind of did a lot of harm to the line. It felt like the Star Wars prequels in a way to me in that it reconceptualized a lot of the setting after it into relation to it, and that wasn't in itself a good thing.<br /> <br /> There were also just parts badly written and those often depended on the specific part. For instnace, in <b>Lands of Creation</b> each chapter was written by different authors and it showed. The South, West, and East were written with this &quot;resent just examples, let players fill in.&quot; The North and Blessed Isle were written as &quot;There are X kingdoms, here's who rules them, that's it.&quot; This stood out ot me then a lot. I also think that despite the emphasis of diversity, the First Age felt pretty homogenous. It didn't use its 3500 years great I think, but hte nature of the product probably wouldn't have let it. And even some of that didn't work well when you did have good Direction stuff, like having to find origins for various mutants in Creation here (dune people and Djala probably didn't need origin sotries as slave races). Also whoever thought needing basically Lintha True Brujah living on an island was a great idea needs questioning.<br /> <br /> It also I think solidified a few conceptual things of power, the relation of the Exalted, and so on in ways that were both outgrowths of 2e up to that point, and continued onward. We got Essence 6+ Charms that were basically sorcery spells because &quot;Solar Circle Sorcery only went to Essence 5&quot; and so we saw a depreciation of sorcery's importance over artifice that started in <b>Wonders of the Lost Age</b>. The blood purity stuff started in <b>MoEP: Dragon-Blooded</b> continued with the canonization of everyone being legendary breeding and miscongenity with mortals being a degradation, and the introduction of Purity keyword stuff which in hindsight, not a great idea. The population of DBs being over a million also does a lot with reinforcing DBs as failures/fuckups/loosers/degenerate/barely Exalted that 2e was running the ball with too. Sidereals not getting any support initially was also kind of one of those &quot;Wait what?&quot; things. Hell, there was even the start of what amounts to a Wiki editor's war in <b>Guide to Meru</b> where the author wrote how Exalts went crazy when their Incarna died...which then led to something later being written to counter that.<br /> <br /> Something else kind of more subtle to me was that it was a highlight of 2e going a bit conservative on its gender politics. Save for Neph's stuff in the West, literally every single Lunar-Solar pair in the First Age was a man and a woman married or at least implied to be so. This is besides things like generally just bad NPCs (Desus and Lilith were pretty cringy, the pushing of Black Shattered Ice as the Lover was unneeded, being cute on Chejob being exactly one year from dying in modern time, or Admiral Arkhadi being a rapist.)<br /> <br /> Mechanciswise, got not much to say. I think Essence 6+ as a paradim from 1e and into 2e was kind of busted an dthis kind of highlighted that in spades. SOme cool Charms, especially for DBs, though. And the later errata gave us Throne Shadow for Sidereals.<br /> <br /> There's a few good ideas scattered about, note. Some locations had some potential to be lifted, I liked the implicaiton of Gaia having more souls in there, and such. But as a whole, I think it as noted is very much a product of its edition. It culminated a lot before it, established a lot that would build on it later, and in general condified 2e as very much its own thing different from 1e and which 3e was rebooting from for me. I was lukewarm on it when it came out even though I was still pretty much in get everything for Exalted mode. I think I was excited more by people working on it though than the product itself and that I mostly remember positive bits to the parts Neph wrote to me indicates that it was more something I wanted for him writing it than as a product I wanted in itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-20T11:29:44-07:00","id":1409394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1409384#post1409384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot of my antipathy towards Dreams of the First Age has come from actually trying to engage it as a playable setting and realising that despite having two books worth of content it's badly lacking.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay. I was very new to tabletop gaming in general when I read it, so I didn\u2019t pick up on that. What makes it so badly lacking?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-20T11:31:23-07:00","id":1409396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1409380#post1409380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pretty sure those bits of toxic memetic fluff were doing their tasteless job a bunch of books before DotFA, harkening to at least CoCD1 in the case of the Dragon-Blooded, probably even before in the case of Lilith &amp; Desus. In fact, ain't Desus gone from canon in 3e? If so, honestly good riddance.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Agreed, on oh-so many levels - the accessing Abyssal charms one i used as springboard for a major &amp;quot;Deathlord but not&amp;quot; npc i would introduce in my games, among other things. And i mine Glories for inspiration to this day even while making no appearance of the Incarna whatsoever. It's a great book indeed that delivers the mythic in a manner that only Scion comes close to in its own way i guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>They did drop Desus from 3e canon. And definitely good riddance. That plotline always made me uncomfortable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-20T12:09:10-07:00","id":1409406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1409396#post1409396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They did drop Desus from 3e canon. And definitely good riddance. That plotline always made me uncomfortable.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Even though i did use it as a element in a PC's background (twice in fact) yeah, canon is much better off without it.<br /> <br /> I'm also very, very happy with the fact we are getting some love for the Shogunate and &quot;Age of Sorrows&quot; with empire-building &amp; toppling, acts of derring-do and all that jazz in 3e.<br /> <br /> Seriously, i once wrote a major antagonist NPC entirely inspired by my <b>vitriolic</b> hatred of the &quot;everything relevant is somehow derived of the 1st Age/Xogunate &amp; Age of Sorrows are speedbumps/stepping stones for glorious solar return&quot; stance of so many writers in 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 08-20-2020, 03:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-20T14:57:40-07:00","id":1409423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1409406#post1409406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Even though i did use it as a element in a PC's background (twice in fact) yeah, canon is much better off without it.<br /> <br /> I'm also very, very happy with the fact we are getting some love for the Shogunate and &amp;quot;Age of Sorrows&amp;quot; with empire-building &amp; toppling, acts of derring-do and all that jazz in 3e.<br /> <br /> Seriously, i once wrote a major antagonist NPC entirely inspired by my <b>vitriolic</b> hatred of the &amp;quot;everything relevant is somehow derived of the 1st Age/Xogunate &amp; Age of Sorrows are speedbumps/stepping stones for glorious solar return&amp;quot; stance of so many writers in 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with you. That attitude is very Solar-centric. I like the Shogunate and the Age of Sorrows too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-20T19:13:19-07:00","id":1409445,"title":"","content":"I think it's sick as hell outside of the bits of 2e lore that pretty much everyone agreed were dumb as hell like its insane anti-Terrestrial bent. It's still canon to me, dammit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","name":"Frostav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-20T22:10:55-07:00","id":1409469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1409406#post1409406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously, i once wrote a major antagonist NPC entirely inspired by my <b>vitriolic</b> hatred of the &amp;quot;everything relevant is somehow derived of the 1st Age/Xogunate &amp; Age of Sorrows are speedbumps/stepping stones for glorious solar return&amp;quot; stance of so many writers in 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>This, so much this.<br /> <br /> Turning Mount Metagalapa from a unique place to &quot;well jeez, if you swept the dust and civilization that's accrued in there over the years, you'd have the amazing Battlestation it's meant to be.&quot;<br /> <br /> Also turning Icemind from an irreproducible wonder to &quot;lol two dragonblooded found the power button for a common desktop in a drunken stupor and turned it on, how cute&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-21T01:11:46-07:00","id":1409484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1409423#post1409423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree with you. That attitude is very Solar-centric. I like the Shogunate and the Age of Sorrows too.</div> </div> </div> </div>That it comes after and is more of a savage time than the civilized glory of Atlantis &amp; Lemuria does not make the Hyborian Age any less awesome.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1409469#post1409469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This, so much this.<br /> <br /> Turning Mount Metagalapa from a unique place to &quot;well jeez, if you swept the dust and civilization that's accrued in there over the years, you'd have the amazing Battlestation it's meant to be.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>As a crazy off-the-cuff reveal in the middle of a campagn it's fine. As an implied piece of canon, definitely not so much. But then hindsight is 20/20 in those things i guess.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1409469#post1409469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also turning Icemind from an irreproducible wonder to &quot;lol two dragonblooded found the power button for a common desktop in a drunken stupor and turned it on, how cute&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Always made my utmost efforts to ignore all but the loosest associations between Icemind and I Am, that was already something of a twist on Eyem from one of the &quot;Records of the Before&quot; pieces in the Aspectbooks, might be said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 08-21-2020, 04:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-21T02:04:30-07:00","id":1409494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1409394#post1409394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay. I was very new to tabletop gaming in general when I read it, so I didn\u2019t pick up on that. What makes it so badly lacking?</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically the supplement doesn't use the space it has very well and the setting presented feels like the result of a bunch of compromises that didn't really make anyone happy.<br /> <br /> When it first came out a lot of Celestial players jumped at the chance to play characters who enjoyed similar levels of privilege and magical artifice to Dynasts or to play absurdly high essence PCs but instead found themselves in a late First Age setting where the greatest enemy was the growing ennui of a world that's increasingly becoming unable to challenge them and themselves.<br /> <br /> If you wanted to play a Dragon-Blooded then the books barely talk about them. You're going to have to make up your Gens and its customs, figure out your own answers for what it's like to grow up as a First Age Dragon-Blooded when there's over a million of them because the books give you <b>nothing </b>to work with. It's particularly egregious when you realise we as readers know things about Desus' private life that he would suicide us in order to prevent from getting out and tarnishing his reputation, but we don't know the name of the Dragon-Blooded family that's sworn to him or where he rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-21T02:47:19-07:00","id":1409503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1409494#post1409494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you wanted to play a Dragon-Blooded then the books barely talk about them. You're going to have to make up your Gens and its customs, figure out your own answers for what it's like to grow up as a First Age Dragon-Blooded when there's over a million of them because the books give you <b>nothing </b>to work with. It's particularly egregious when you realise we as readers know things about Desus' private life that he would suicide us in order to prevent from getting out and tarnishing his reputation, but we don't know the name of the Dragon-Blooded family that's sworn to him or where he rules.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Meanwhile we get to be presented of Marama, that would give the name for a major shadowland of the North, as the name of a gens of sex workers made to exploit tourism to Ombar Shambal, a holy city.<br /> <br /> (i really miss an eyeroll emote right now) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-20-2020, 08:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-21T05:20:53-07:00","id":1409521,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1147_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1147\" data-vbnamecard=\"1147\">Baaldam</a> when you put it that way, I totally agree<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7\" data-vbnamecard=\"7\">Lioness</a> what you\u2019re saying makes a lot of sense","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-21T05:41:36-07:00","id":1409529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1409521#post1409521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1147_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1147\" data-vbnamecard=\"1147\">Baaldam</a> when you put it that way, I totally agree<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7\" data-vbnamecard=\"7\">Lioness</a> what you\u2019re saying makes a lot of sense</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Truth be told, i've been thinking of doing a rewrite of Marama's Fel.<br /> <br /> One where Marama, instead of a unemployed sex worker turned monk turned revolutionary general venting all its resentment of created races, was a sorcerer doing a series of experiments with those inhuman races in some cases trying to replicate, mix or uplilf them through the use of all sorts of elemental essence and sorcerous interactions.<br /> <br /> And so it did for decades or centuries, with varying but mostly successful results (at least in keeping all those beings distracted and pacified for the Shogunate), until it decided to do a great mass suicide ritual working with its throngs of awed/abused/brainwashed subjects and their families, leading to the formation of the Fell (mostly) as we know it.<br /> <br /> A way to both empower the narrative of the shadowland and make it sound <i>a little</i> more like a place that might challenge not one but two Deathlords. Leaving in the air the possibility of a nebulous sorcerous/necromantic working of unknown objective &amp; powers and the shade of a dead dragon-blooded sorcerer secretly ruling a nation of almost-elemental undead, well, is one or two steps up in that direction i hope.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 11-05-2023, 07:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-21T05:49:30-07:00","id":1409532,"title":"","content":"There are some really conceptually cool Charms in the errataed DotFA (which is the version now available on Drivethru) - to the point that 3E pretty much folded them into the core game via Sorcerous Workings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-21T07:51:38-07:00","id":1409558,"title":"","content":"I think the sidebar on page 58 of Lords of Creation. <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> Charms running from Essence 1 to 5 are detailed <br /> on page 184 of Exalted.<br /> Charms having Essence minimums from 1 to 5 <br /> encompass the complete array of effects for which the <br /> Solars were given purpose. Having conquered chaos <br /> and ascended to rulership of Creation, Solars expand <br /> to represent a purpose for which there was no design. <br /> Charms beyond the Essence minimum of 5 suggest <br /> a force for which there is no peer, and a measure for <br /> which there is no call. In short, these effects equip the <br /> Solars with a new array of effects of such magnitude and <br /> scope that there could be no known reason. Beyond <br /> this point, Solars transcend humanity, expand their <br /> notice beyond the core of existence, bargain with <br /> incomprehensible forces, and build new worlds\u2014if <br /> only to have more to conquer.<br /> Charms with an Essence minimum of 6 leave be-<br /> hind worldly miracles\u2014the Exalt now engages in the <br /> work of gods. Her power redefines her standing among <br /> the Exalted, and it is on the back of these wonders that <br /> an Age may be built.<br /> Charms with an Essence minimum of 7 depict <br /> the authorial primacy of one who knows no value she <br /> cannot change and no limit she cannot reach. These <br /> miracles leave marks on the world that last for untold <br /> generations, each application a legend unto itself. The <br /> holy might contained by these Charms evoke such awe <br /> and terror that the Celestial Exalted look upon them <br /> with shocked remove.<br /> Charms with an Essence minimum of 8 touch the <br /> very foundation of the universe. The Solar lays hands <br /> upon the forces of the very cosmos, and they recognize <br /> in her Essence a peer. <br /> Charms with an Essence minimum of 9 affect all <br /> the heavenly glory of the sun unbound. Solar power <br /> expands almost beyond the capacity of the world to <br /> contain it. What is the possible purpose of such great <br /> and terrible power?<br /> Charms with an Essence minimum of 10 denote <br /> powers beyond those which forged the universe. Not <br /> even the Primordials fully understand Essence 10; at <br /> this level of effect, the intellects which defined ex-<br /> istence find themselves in the position of discovery. <br /> What challenges even the Primordials, a Solar may <br /> come naturally to grasp and engender: power beyond <br /> all reason.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Which to me is like this;<br /> <br /> DotFA: Essence 5 is the essence of the greatest heroes of the world. Essence 5 is what you need to do anything. Essence six is beyond that. As Essence increases past six the world itself and everything in it becomes nothing to you.<br /> <br /> Me: Okay so what that that mean?<br /> <br /> DotFA: Yeah what DOES it mean?<br /> <br /> Me: No, I mean like, how do I ST for a game with Essence 10 PCs that are beyond even Primordials?<br /> <br /> DotFA: Now THAT is an intriguing question, isn\u2019t it?<br /> <br /> Me: You have even a hint of an answer?<br /> <br /> DotFA: What do you think I am?<br /> <br /> Me: An RPG rules/setting book- wait, hang on, aren\u2019t the Deathlords Essence 10 with all solar charms that they meet the minimums for and more?<br /> <br /> DotFA: correct.<br /> <br /> Me: So in the second age, where most games are set, there\u2019s thirteen dudes walking around who are greater than the primordials, and to whom the entire rest of the world is pathetically, meaninglessly weak?<br /> <br /> DotFA: Indeed, the Deathlords possess powers FAR beyond the capacity for anyone or anything to challenge them, even remotely. Except for people like Chejop Kejak, he can. <br /> <br /> Me: So when the 2e corebook promised that the returning Solars, who are Essence 2-5 at best, would either destroy the world or save it that was...?<br /> <br /> DotFA: A total lie, yes. Players like Kejak and the First and Forsaken Lion treat entire directions of Creation as pawns in their chess game.<br /> <br /> Me: Please tell me how you expect me to play this and use the setting info as a Storyteller.<br /> <br /> DotFA: Okay, okay, I\u2019ll give you a little hint, because I\u2019m nice not because it\u2019s my job. You know those tens of thousands of words you\u2019ve read about the setting? About the gods, elementals, spirits, kingdoms like Paragon, Whitewall, Nexus, and Coral?<br /> <br /> Me: Okay yeah?<br /> <br /> DotFA: Treat that like we told you the intricate social networks and habits of primary school children. If you want a place like Nexus or Whitewall to matter, you can say an Essence 10 Solar survivor from the first age lives there, that\u2019ll make it important. <br /> <br /> Me: So a primordial is just hiding out in any city I want to mean anything.<br /> <br /> DotFA: Not a primordial, greater than a primordial. He or she is just hiding out there for some reason which you\u2019ll have to think up yourself.<br /> <br /> Me: This is dumb.<br /> <br /> <br /> And ultimately that kind of thinking is what lead especially late 2e into being a game where nothing but Exalted mattered, and nothing but Solars REALLY mattered, especially ones who started at Essence 5 with Divine Transcendence of (Ability) and that other cap bursted from Glories. It made for a ton of frustration, I\u2019m glad it\u2019s over, and I hope it never comes back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-21T07:56:15-07:00","id":1409560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1409503#post1409503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meanwhile we get to be presented of Marama, that would give the name for a major shadowland of the North, as the name of a gens of sex workers made to exploit turism to Ombar Shambal, a holy city.<br /> <br /> (i really miss an eyeroll emote right now) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I really like that.<br /> <br /> I like that the Dragon-Blooded we're conceived as elemental super soldiers, but 2E left them with no great war to fight, sidelined into courtesans and chauffeurs... then displaced by the created races. It makes the Usurpation more... heroic? Like it's restoring the natural balance...<br /> <br /> When you're living on your knees you RISE UP!<br /> <br /> RISE ABOVE! WE'RE GONNA RISE ABOVE!<br /> <br /> The tale of an unemployed sex worker turned monk turned revolutionary general speaks to me about how far the Solars had debased Creation. And The Fell, is a tragic lesson in the language of the unheard.<br /> <br /> Awesome Dragon-Blooded nobility committing to the Usurpation because they don't sit quite as high up the Exalted totem pole as they'd like is kinda &quot;meh&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-21T08:36:58-07:00","id":1409567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1409560#post1409560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really like that.<br /> <br /> I like that the Dragon-Blooded we're conceived as elemental super soldiers, but 2E left them with no great war to fight, sidelined into courtesans and chauffeurs... then displaced by the created races. It makes the Usurpation more... heroic? Like it's restoring the natural balance...<br /> <br /> When you're living on your knees you RISE UP!<br /> <br /> RISE ABOVE! WE'RE GONNA RISE ABOVE!<br /> <br /> The tale of an unemployed sex worker turned monk turned revolutionary general speaks to me about how far the Solars had debased Creation. And The Fell, is a tragic lesson in the language of the unheard.<br /> <br /> Awesome Dragon-Blooded nobility committing to the Usurpation because they don't sit quite as high up the Exalted totem pole as they'd like is kinda &quot;meh&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>To me this is an example of example of DotFA trying to touch all the bases to please everyone and failing miserably. Here's what another 2e books had to say about the late First Age.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Compass Blessed Isle, page 10</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shortly before the Usurpation, almost every mortal living in the Blessed Isle knew someone who had been killed or horribly used by the Solar Exalted. As a result, the cities of the Blessed Isle became centers for a carefully hidden resistance against the excesses of the Solar Deliberative. Knowing the horrible fates that awaited anyone caught in a conspiracy against the Solar Exalted, the rebels and dissidents held secret meetings, where most members wore masks and otherwise disguised their identities. These precautions made sure that conspirators caught by the Solars could not reveal the identities of other rebels, even when powerful Charms forced them to love their Solar interrogators with undying passion.</div> </div> </div> </div> We didn't get that First Age because it would've been even more off-putting to people who wanted to play a Solar but as a playable setting it would've had way more purpose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 08-21-2020, 11:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-21T10:04:37-07:00","id":1409584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1409558#post1409558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the sidebar on page 58 of Lords of Creation.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> Charms running from Essence 1 to 5 are detailed<br /> on page 184 of Exalted.<br /> Charms having Essence minimums from 1 to 5<br /> encompass the complete array of effects for which the<br /> Solars were given purpose. Having conquered chaos<br /> and ascended to rulership of Creation, Solars expand<br /> to represent a purpose for which there was no design.<br /> Charms beyond the Essence minimum of 5 suggest<br /> a force for which there is no peer, and a measure for<br /> which there is no call. In short, these effects equip the<br /> Solars with a new array of effects of such magnitude and<br /> scope that there could be no known reason. Beyond<br /> this point, Solars transcend humanity, expand their<br /> notice beyond the core of existence, bargain with<br /> incomprehensible forces, and build new worlds\u2014if<br /> only to have more to conquer.<br /> Charms with an Essence minimum of 6 leave be-<br /> hind worldly miracles\u2014the Exalt now engages in the<br /> work of gods. Her power redefines her standing among<br /> the Exalted, and it is on the back of these wonders that<br /> an Age may be built.<br /> Charms with an Essence minimum of 7 depict<br /> the authorial primacy of one who knows no value she<br /> cannot change and no limit she cannot reach. These<br /> miracles leave marks on the world that last for untold<br /> generations, each application a legend unto itself. The<br /> holy might contained by these Charms evoke such awe<br /> and terror that the Celestial Exalted look upon them<br /> with shocked remove.<br /> Charms with an Essence minimum of 8 touch the<br /> very foundation of the universe. The Solar lays hands<br /> upon the forces of the very cosmos, and they recognize<br /> in her Essence a peer.<br /> Charms with an Essence minimum of 9 affect all<br /> the heavenly glory of the sun unbound. Solar power<br /> expands almost beyond the capacity of the world to<br /> contain it. What is the possible purpose of such great<br /> and terrible power?<br /> Charms with an Essence minimum of 10 denote<br /> powers beyond those which forged the universe. Not<br /> even the Primordials fully understand Essence 10; at<br /> this level of effect, the intellects which defined ex-<br /> istence find themselves in the position of discovery.<br /> What challenges even the Primordials, a Solar may<br /> come naturally to grasp and engender: power beyond<br /> all reason.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Which to me is like this;<br /> <br /> DotFA: Essence 5 is the essence of the greatest heroes of the world. Essence 5 is what you need to do anything. Essence six is beyond that. As Essence increases past six the world itself and everything in it becomes nothing to you.<br /> <br /> Me: Okay so what that that mean?<br /> <br /> DotFA: Yeah what DOES it mean?<br /> <br /> Me: No, I mean like, how do I ST for a game with Essence 10 PCs that are beyond even Primordials?<br /> <br /> DotFA: Now THAT is an intriguing question, isn\u2019t it?<br /> <br /> Me: You have even a hint of an answer?<br /> <br /> DotFA: What do you think I am?<br /> <br /> Me: An RPG rules/setting book- wait, hang on, aren\u2019t the Deathlords Essence 10 with all solar charms that they meet the minimums for and more?<br /> <br /> DotFA: correct.<br /> <br /> Me: So in the second age, where most games are set, there\u2019s thirteen dudes walking around who are greater than the primordials, and to whom the entire rest of the world is pathetically, meaninglessly weak?<br /> <br /> DotFA: Indeed, the Deathlords possess powers FAR beyond the capacity for anyone or anything to challenge them, even remotely. Except for people like Chejop Kejak, he can.<br /> <br /> Me: So when the 2e corebook promised that the returning Solars, who are Essence 2-5 at best, would either destroy the world or save it that was...?<br /> <br /> DotFA: A total lie, yes. Players like Kejak and the First and Forsaken Lion treat entire directions of Creation as pawns in their chess game.<br /> <br /> Me: Please tell me how you expect me to play this and use the setting info as a Storyteller.<br /> <br /> DotFA: Okay, okay, I\u2019ll give you a little hint, because I\u2019m nice not because it\u2019s my job. You know those tens of thousands of words you\u2019ve read about the setting? About the gods, elementals, spirits, kingdoms like Paragon, Whitewall, Nexus, and Coral?<br /> <br /> Me: Okay yeah?<br /> <br /> DotFA: Treat that like we told you the intricate social networks and habits of primary school children. If you want a place like Nexus or Whitewall to matter, you can say an Essence 10 Solar survivor from the first age lives there, that\u2019ll make it important.<br /> <br /> Me: So a primordial is just hiding out in any city I want to mean anything.<br /> <br /> DotFA: Not a primordial, greater than a primordial. He or she is just hiding out there for some reason which you\u2019ll have to think up yourself.<br /> <br /> Me: This is dumb.<br /> <br /> <br /> And ultimately that kind of thinking is what lead especially late 2e into being a game where nothing but Exalted mattered, and nothing but Solars REALLY mattered, especially ones who started at Essence 5 with Divine Transcendence of (Ability) and that other cap bursted from Glories. It made for a ton of frustration, I\u2019m glad it\u2019s over, and I hope it never comes back.</div> </div> </div> </div>At first I read only your explanation and then I went to read the quote. I must say, it really looks like the writer is making fun of people that wants to &quot;power level&quot; because it's so absurd and convoluted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-21T10:29:45-07:00","id":1409588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1409584#post1409584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> At first I read only your explanation and then I went to read the quote. I must say, it really looks like the writer is making fun of people that wants to &amp;quot;power level&amp;quot; because it's so absurd and convoluted.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, you\u2019d think that, right? Well later on in the book there\u2019s an Essence 8 charm which lets you sing a song and over the course of a minute cast an entire city into Hell, and an Essence 7 Lore charm that lets you alter the fundamental laws of the universe, for example \u201call armies that march to war will be incinerated by pillars of white fire. This takes effect over all of Creation, all adjoining worlds, and even worlds that the exalted have yet to discover.\u201d There we go, no more armies anywhere. Yes, that is a valid use of that charm, although fully integrating it with Creation requires some higher Essence magic, keeping in mind that charm is only Essence 7. I\u2019m not even saying that\u2019s a bad idea for a game, but for one it kind of messed with the Exalted setting, and for another there\u2019s basically no support for that kind of stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-21T11:02:01-07:00","id":1409591,"title":"","content":"Yeah at that point there are no rules or whatever it's just use Charm X the game ends. Better play Godsend","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-21T11:26:18-07:00","id":1409594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1409591#post1409591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah at that point there are no rules or whatever it's just use Charm X the game ends. Better play Godsend</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, here\u2019s another one. The First and Forsaken Lion is a huge danger in the South because in the Underworld he has an army of undead over 200,000 strong and an artifact airship that\u2019s nearly a mile long called <i>Final Maelstrom</i> the only thing stopping him is that he hasn\u2019t found a Shadowland yet large enough to bring that force through. <br /> <br /> Yeah, that sounds like a good antagonist.<br /> <br /> Yeah.<br /> <br /> Except he has Melee 10 and Solar melee charms. One of which allows him to attack all enemies within 30 miles, safeguarding allies from this attack, add 20 dice to his attacks, and wield a weapon that adds +10 to the base weapon\u2019s accuracy, damage, defense, and rate, and double 10s on damage. That\u2019s three charms which are Essence 6 and 7. He could combine them with other printed charms, and also unprinted Essence 10 ones. He needs this zombie army why? Does he just want <i>Final Maelstrom</i> because it\u2019s a sick ride and he wants to look cool while conquering the south? He could slay all of Chiaroscuro in three minutes with that combo, and he\u2019s not even flexing to do it! In fact doing that would actually create a shadowland large enough to bring his army though! <br /> <br /> I think you\u2019ve mentioned you weren\u2019t around much for 2e before, but this is basically where most of the hate comes from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-21T12:49:18-07:00","id":1409609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1409594#post1409594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh yeah, here\u2019s another one. The First and Forsaken Lion is a huge danger in the South because in the Underworld he has an army of undead over 200,000 strong and an artifact airship that\u2019s nearly a mile long called <i>Final Maelstrom</i> the only thing stopping him is that he hasn\u2019t found a Shadowland yet large enough to bring that force through.<br /> <br /> Yeah, that sounds like a good antagonist.<br /> <br /> Yeah.<br /> <br /> Except he has Melee 10 and Solar melee charms. One of which allows him to attack all enemies within 30 miles, safeguarding allies from this attack, add 20 dice to his attacks, and wield a weapon that adds +10 to the base weapon\u2019s accuracy, damage, defense, and rate, and double 10s on damage. That\u2019s three charms which are Essence 6 and 7. He could combine them with other printed charms, and also unprinted Essence 10 ones. He needs this zombie army why? Does he just want <i>Final Maelstrom</i> because it\u2019s a sick ride and he wants to look cool while conquering the south? He could slay all of Chiaroscuro in three minutes with that combo, and he\u2019s not even flexing to do it! In fact doing that would actually create a shadowland large enough to bring his army though!<br /> <br /> I think you\u2019ve mentioned you weren\u2019t around much for 2e before, but this is basically where most of the hate comes from.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah I think I'm pretty happy I wasn't here for 2e. Some things definitively went strange !","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-21T13:46:18-07:00","id":1409620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1409560#post1409560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really like that.<br /> <br /> I like that the Dragon-Blooded we're conceived as elemental super soldiers, but 2E left them with no great war to fight, sidelined into courtesans and chauffeurs... then displaced by the created races. It makes the Usurpation more... heroic? Like it's restoring the natural balance...<br /> <br /> When you're living on your knees you RISE UP!<br /> <br /> RISE ABOVE! WE'RE GONNA RISE ABOVE!<br /> <br /> The tale of an unemployed sex worker turned monk turned revolutionary general speaks to me about how far the Solars had debased Creation. And The Fell, is a tragic lesson in the language of the unheard.<br /> <br /> Awesome Dragon-Blooded nobility committing to the Usurpation because they don't sit quite as high up the Exalted totem pole as they'd like is kinda &quot;meh&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh, when was the whole &quot;going stark having mad &amp; corrupt superpowered competing overlords of Creation&quot; motivating the Usurpation was scrapped? I seem to forget. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> But back on what you were saying, i can see how at first glance my rushed and broad strokes summary of Marama's story could be seen as a pretty decent seed for a wrathful revolutionary kind of character narrative.<br /> <br /> Main problem? It kind of comes crashing down hard when you look at what it informs of the setting in matters of her gens, past solar master and other issues, like her own stats.<br /> <br /> Because the Essence 5, Breeding 5, Manipulation 5, Appearance 6, Performance/Presence/Socialize 5, Bureaucracy 4 courtesan/majordomo was not only <i>utterly bested</i> by lord Tyraeth's lunar mate marriage anniversary servitor....<br /> <br /> (she made a 2nd circle demons' amalgam or what? also, kind of weird gift when <i>you have a whole gens</i> to deal with it already, savage slap in the face that...)<br /> <br /> ... but <i>somehow</i> can't find work in another role in her own gens (guess they are all adamant grade @$$e$...), on some other exalt's retinue - because apparently her reputation (2) as exotic courtesan makes it impossible (even though few exalts are prudes <i>and</i> she has Larceny 4, that can offer her <i>extra</i> tricks to get around this) - <b>or</b> seduce her way into marrying on other gentes, as lots of DBs should jump at the chance <b><i>even</i></b> if she had no actual skills and power, because she's crazy hot (literally) and has ginormous.... breeding!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (not even going into the fact Marama <b>also</b> has Athletics, Integrity, Linguistcs, Melee and Resistance 5, meaning she <b>can</b> go from personal snu-snu trainer into bodyguard/sword companion without even a 6-month Tiger Warrior Training course)<br /> <br /> So, as presented we have severe cases of celestial masters <b>and</b> family holding the idiot/jerk@$$ ball to make her story work, with the bonus of her actual sheet making everything more absurd, due to how utterly overqualified she should actually be (i'll admit i haven't really delved into her charmset, but she has at least one Ess4 charm, a melee one, called out).<br /> <br /> Also, let me say it again and try to get across some salient bits - <i>gens of high-quality sex workers</i><b><i> specialized on exalted ascetics/penitents in pilgrimage to <u>one holy city</u></i></b>.<br /> <br /> A little too niche/localized/gratuitously edgy to near ineffectiveness for defining feature/role of <i>a whole gens</i> perhaps?<br /> <br /> <i>Thankfully</i>, for a a saving grace of sorts, the text does inform us the Anjei gens has served Lord Tyraeth as majordomos for four generations, what with DBs could be anything from literally 80 years/four generations to four dragon-blooded lifespans, aka 100-1200 years. Either way, at least it's definitely stated they are <b>not</b> one of the mammoth/ancient gens harkening to the armies of primordial war generals or somesuch.<br /> <br /> (In hindsight i'm so<i> not ok at all</i> with 2e imagery/meme of each Solar-Lunar bonded pair having a whole legion of dragon-blooded under their command during the Primordial War it ain't even funny)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 08-21-2020, 06:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-21T16:30:08-07:00","id":1409644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1409560#post1409560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really like that.<br /> <br /> I like that the Dragon-Blooded we're conceived as elemental super soldiers, but 2E left them with no great war to fight, sidelined into courtesans and chauffeurs... then displaced by the created races. It makes the Usurpation more... heroic? Like it's restoring the natural balance...<br /> <br /> When you're living on your knees you RISE UP!<br /> <br /> RISE ABOVE! WE'RE GONNA RISE ABOVE!<br /> <br /> The tale of an unemployed sex worker turned monk turned revolutionary general speaks to me about how far the Solars had debased Creation. And The Fell, is a tragic lesson in the language of the unheard.<br /> <br /> Awesome Dragon-Blooded nobility committing to the Usurpation because they don't sit quite as high up the Exalted totem pole as they'd like is kinda &amp;quot;meh&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Marama's story COULD have been about her realizing the Solars used and discarded her, and realizing that they were doing the same to the Terrestrial host and Creation as a whole, and deciding that ENOUGH WAS ENOUGH!<br /> <br /> Instead, it was about her being discarded by her solar master, and hating created races for stealing her master's preference. Then founding a servitor-murdering gang while working as an escort in a holy city, then hating solars in a psycho ex-gf way, then commiting genocide because of psycho ex-gf hate.<br /> <br /> Your take works better for what we knew about Marama's Fel at the time than what was given in DotFA, because the perspective is better.<br /> <br /> Oh well, at least we got Saibok. There wasn't really that much to do with him, but I liked how chill his entry was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23964-el-barto","name":"El Barto","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-21T19:29:37-07:00","id":1409675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1409594#post1409594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh yeah, here\u2019s another one. The First and Forsaken Lion is a huge danger in the South because in the Underworld he has an army of undead over 200,000 strong and an artifact airship that\u2019s nearly a mile long called <i>Final Maelstrom</i> the only thing stopping him is that he hasn\u2019t found a Shadowland yet large enough to bring that force through. <br /> <br /> Yeah, that sounds like a good antagonist.<br /> <br /> Yeah.<br /> <br /> Except he has Melee 10 and Solar melee charms. One of which allows him to attack all enemies within 30 miles, safeguarding allies from this attack, add 20 dice to his attacks, and wield a weapon that adds +10 to the base weapon\u2019s accuracy, damage, defense, and rate, and double 10s on damage. That\u2019s three charms which are Essence 6 and 7. He could combine them with other printed charms, and also unprinted Essence 10 ones. He needs this zombie army why? Does he just want <i>Final Maelstrom</i> because it\u2019s a sick ride and he wants to look cool while conquering the south? He could slay all of Chiaroscuro in three minutes with that combo, and he\u2019s not even flexing to do it! In fact doing that would actually create a shadowland large enough to bring his army though! <br /> <br /> I think you\u2019ve mentioned you weren\u2019t around much for 2e before, but this is basically where most of the hate comes from.</div> </div> </div> </div>\ud83d\ude02\ud83d\ude02\ud83d\ude02\ud83d\ude02<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1121_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1121\" data-vbnamecard=\"1121\">DrLoveMonkey</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7\" data-vbnamecard=\"7\">Lioness</a> has anyone ever tried to cross over the Solar Exalted with novas from Aberrant?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-21T19:47:49-07:00","id":1409680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1409675#post1409675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \ud83d\ude02\ud83d\ude02\ud83d\ude02\ud83d\ude02<br /> <br /> <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> has anyone ever tried to cross over the Solar Exalted with novas from Aberrant?</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m sadly not familiar with Aberrant. That up there is Essence 7 out of 10 though remember. Essence 10 Solars from DotFA might be closer to characters from Nobilis, like where they can punch the concepts of Tuesdays out of existence, and now every event that happened on a Tuesday now didn\u2019t happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-22T01:29:54-07:00","id":1409715,"title":"","content":"Thank you. I\u2019ve never read Nobilis, but Aberrant is a game about godlike superheroes who eventually degenerate and go crazy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-22T01:40:01-07:00","id":1409716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>El Barto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1409644#post1409644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Marama's story COULD have been about her realizing the Solars used and discarded her, and realizing that they were doing the same to the Terrestrial host and Creation as a whole, and deciding that ENOUGH WAS ENOUGH!</div> </div> </div> </div>And <i>if</i> the devs are reading this, I'd prefer Marama get the &quot;Raksi&quot; treatment of being rewritten to be more nuanced, than the &quot;Lilith&quot; treatment of being completely rewritten from the ground up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1409620#post1409620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Uh, when was the whole &quot;going stark having mad &amp; corrupt superpowered competing overlords of Creation&quot; motivating the Usurpation was scrapped? I seem to forget. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> A little too niche/localized/gratuitously edgy to near ineffectiveness for defining feature/role of <i>a whole gens</i> perhaps?</div> </div> </div> </div>What did the Solars do in the First Age to provoke the Usurpation? Published 3E text sources only please. I got one generic paragraph on page 20 of the Corebook. There's literally nothing in What Fire Has Wrought or Fangs at the Gate. CoCD: Blessed Isle said every mortal on the Isle had suffered under the Solars. The Realm only speaks of the Usurpation twice -- once is to mention the Solar dead, and the other is... this: &quot;Third Daughter won\u2019t forgive Heaven or the Realm until the suffering meted out to the Dragon-Blooded and the Sidereals equals that which they incicted in the Usurpation.&quot;<br /> <br /> In 3E*, Dragon-Blooded aren't an oppressed underclass overthrowing their masters. They're respected, courted, warriors who are wrecking the High First Age with their own constant bloody warfare... and who continue to do so after overthrowing the Solars. And their motivation for overthrowing the Solars? Well in WFHW it's &quot;Because the Sidereals said so&quot;.<br /> <br /> And maybe this is a racial issue, IDK, but corrupt masters engineering a social system where the absolute, unquestionable brilliance of their slaves is actively overlooked and maligned speaks to me.<br /> <br /> My ancestors who were priests and princes and poets were stripped of their dignity and forced into fields to pick crops because they were forced into a system that didn't think they were good for anything. I see the plight of my people replicated in the Gens.<br /> <br /> And yes, a family of superhumans acting as sex workers for a holy city is on-the-nose. That's the point. That's literally the point.<br /> <br /> *The presentation of the Dragon-Blooded in the Second Age (lore and mechanics) is the best it's ever been. Critacism of their First Age portrayal in 2E is perfectly valid. My point is that there's a massive stylistic difference between 3E and 2E, and which you prefer is a matter of taste.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 08-22-2020, 05:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-22T01:50:22-07:00","id":1409718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1409716#post1409716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the &amp;quot;Lilith&amp;quot; treatment of being completely rewritten from the ground up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the core story of Lilith was always a Lunar who responded to the pain of the Usurpation by spending centuries hiding as an owl.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">My ancestors who were priests and princes and poets were stripped of their dignity and forced into fields to pick crops because they were forced into a system that didn't think they were good for anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where did <i>their</i> food come from?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-22T01:56:47-07:00","id":1409719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1409716#post1409716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And <i>if</i> the devs are reading this, I'd prefer Marama get the &amp;quot;Raksi&amp;quot; treatment of being rewritten to be more nuanced, than the &amp;quot;Lilith&amp;quot; treatment of being completely rewritten from the ground up.<br /> <br /> <br /> What did the Solars do in the First Age to provoke the Usurpation? Published 3E text sources only please. I got one generic paragraph on page 20 of the Corebook.<br /> <br /> And maybe this is a racial issue, IDK, but corrupt masters engineering a social system where the absolute, unquestionable brilliance of their slaves is actively overlooked and maligned speaks to me.<br /> <br /> My ancestors who were priests and princes and poets were stripped of their dignity and forced into fields to pick crops because they were forced into a system that didn't think they were good for anything. I see the plight of my people replicated in the Gens.<br /> <br /> And yes, a family of superhumans acting as sex workers for a holy city is on-the-nose. That's the point. That's literally the point.</div> </div> </div> </div>First paragraph: I agree with you that it\u2019s better to rewrite characters to be more nuanced, but Lilith needed a lot of work.<br /> <br /> Second paragraph: I don\u2019t know exactly what the Solars did to provoke the Usurpation, but I suspect a big part of it was that they treated the Dragon-Blooded like a slave race, or at least like second-class citizens. Also, another big part was that the Solars degenerated and became both decadent and crazy in general.<br /> <br /> Third and fourth paragraphs: Totally agree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-22T02:01:44-07:00","id":1409720,"title":"","content":"One more thing: from the very first time I read it, when I barely knew what Exalted was, the image of Lilith as a strong Lunar lady, an icon of femininity (hence her name), beaten into submission by her boyfriend to the point where her Limit Break is literally called the Whipped Dog, REALLY set my teeth on edge. I\u2019m glad they changed her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-22T02:04:47-07:00","id":1409721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1409718#post1409718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, the core story of Lilith was always a Lunar who responded to the pain of the Usurpation by spending centuries hiding as an owl.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Where did <i>their</i> food come from?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey Isator. I'll take the two week ban.<br /> <br /> Fuck you, you enormous piece of shit.<br /> <br /> How DARE YOU defend chattle slavery in an effort to win a fucking edition war argument.<br /> <br /> Sincerely, fuck yourself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-22T03:51:03-07:00","id":1409730,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Okay, formal warning for the personal attack.<br /> <br /> I'm not banning anyone or ejecting anyone from the thread if we're capable of moving past this. The comment was insensitive in-context and I'd appreciate PMs about if there's some specific coded language at play or what &quot;Where did their food come from?&quot; was going for.<br /> <br /> Edit: Upon additional consideration I am exten</b><b>ding the warning to Isator Levi's post. His post history makes it unlikely this was a racist attack and he's helped me understand what he intended to say, but there was a style of rhetoric at play that contributed to the misunderstanding and on a sensitive matter such as this it's only fair that we all take responsibility for our words. <br /> <br /> Thank you for everyone who helped out in matter. </b></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 08-22-2020, 04:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-22T10:45:28-07:00","id":1409785,"title":"","content":"The three sample Dragon-Blooded were poorly chosen if they were expected to provide insight into what their lives were because of the three only Vagyn Z\u00fb seems 'normal'.<br /> <br /> Saibok Gauto is Dragon-Blooded Methuselah and Anjei Marama is conditioned not to harm a Solar Exalt even if her own life depends on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-22T13:47:48-07:00","id":1409813,"title":"","content":"Thoughts, as a setting: There was a lot of pile-on toward it for being a bit of a &quot;Bright Near Future Anime Sci-Fi&quot; setting. (This was a thing at the time! Seems less so now! For reasons!). Bit of a mouthful to say that but you probably(?) get the point. The pile-on always seemed unfair given how the &quot;Records of the Before&quot; had built up the First Age in the First Edition Aspect Books and so forth, as something roughly like this combined with a &quot;High Fantasy&quot; setting (which in turn has some resonances with a bucolic ideal, I guess somewhat Confucian in resonances that Geoff Grabowski seemed to comment on finding an interesting way to modulate the First Age).<br /> <br /> That aside, I don't think it was very skillfully written, to be honest. It's all a bit referential to earlier Exalted works and lacking in innovation (too much Autochthon, etc), and sort of compresses things together in some senses, rather than opening up space in a useful manner. There are things I think, with hindsight are pretty bad moves (is it really a good idea to suggest the Unconquered Sun at ab initio descended and granted rulership to, like, a single Solar Exalt?) - but that's with hindsight! There seems like some stuff that seems very 2eism - like Wyld Shaping Technique as one of *the* signature Solar things, to the degree they have a whole era of the First Age that's defined by &quot;Solars used Wyld Shaping Technique a *lot*!&quot;. There are some writing style problems I guess as well - some overuse of pseudo-Chinese motifs in naming stands out to me.<br /> <br /> There are definitely some interesting ideas to mine out though (history-wise, I quite like the idea that the Solars went full bonkers when they realized they had lifespans, and the idea of some &quot;harbingers&quot; like the &quot;Time of Cascading Years&quot; or &quot;Wyldhand&quot; is interesting.)<br /> <br /> A lot of the problems with it to me lie in the authors being more constrained to sort of draw together bits of what Geoff Grabowski had dropped over the years, and knit together popular 1e-2e setting elements, and in some senses serve the Age of Sorrows setting. There are some other problems that probably degenerate from how 2e specifically construed the nature of Exalted power and Charms. In many ways it's sort of a setting idea that in an ideal world of unlimited creative resources I'd like to see built with a freer hand - perhaps this is possible within Exalted's mainline world, perhaps better suited to being a &quot;shard&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-22T17:04:21-07:00","id":1409837,"title":"","content":"Loved it. Facet Raven. Queen K'tula. That one time where every Exalt got to be the only Exalt in Creation because time broke and if they saved the world they got to re-merge with the prime timeline. The guidebook to Meru's dripping condescension for mortals. The art! The potential for drama!<br /> <br /> One of my players wishes to ascend to storyteller, and she is set on telling her story in the First Age. I can't think of higher praise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-23T01:47:03-07:00","id":1409866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1409716#post1409716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What did the Solars do in the First Age to provoke the Usurpation? Published 3E text sources only please. I got one generic paragraph on page 20 of the Corebook. There's literally nothing in What Fire Has Wrought or Fangs at the Gate. CoCD: Blessed Isle said every mortal on the Isle had suffered under the Solars. The Realm only speaks of the Usurpation twice -- once is to mention the Solar dead, and the other is... this: &quot;Third Daughter won\u2019t forgive Heaven or the Realm until the suffering meted out to the Dragon-Blooded and the Sidereals equals that which they incicted in the Usurpation.&quot;<br /> <br /> In 3E*, Dragon-Blooded aren't an oppressed underclass overthrowing their masters. They're respected, courted, warriors who are wrecking the High First Age with their own constant bloody warfare... and who continue to do so after overthrowing the Solars. And their motivation for overthrowing the Solars? Well in WFHW it's &quot;Because the Sidereals said so&quot;.<br /> <br /> And maybe this is a racial issue, IDK, but corrupt masters engineering a social system where the absolute, unquestionable brilliance of their slaves is actively overlooked and maligned speaks to me.<br /> <br /> My ancestors who were priests and princes and poets were stripped of their dignity and forced into fields to pick crops because they were forced into a system that didn't think they were good for anything. I see the plight of my people replicated in the Gens.<br /> <br /> And yes, a family of superhumans acting as sex workers for a holy city is on-the-nose. That's the point. That's literally the point.<br /> <br /> *The presentation of the Dragon-Blooded in the Second Age (lore and mechanics) is the best it's ever been. Critacism of their First Age portrayal in 2E is perfectly valid. My point is that there's a massive stylistic difference between 3E and 2E, and which you prefer is a matter of taste.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree the books don't present an explicit &quot;what went wrong scenario&quot;, which is a cool idea I think. I hope for the future if they publish anything concerning the First Age, it'll be mostly apocryphal (or avoid the apparent 2e peculiarity of explaining everything).<br /> <br /> So here's my view on the matter : What I like about 3e is that it doesn't tell us explicitly why the DB did it, which is the opportunity to make it very political and personnal. I've already talked about my headcanons so to me the world was kinda decentralized, with no &quot;global union of Solars to control the world&quot; or whatever. The DB weren't in an especially bad position, except for the fact that everyone (Solars included) was starting to be in a bad position because Solars and Lunars were starting to get devoured by their Curse (Sidereals maybe but I don't know them enough). So they didn't decide to do it for one simple ideological reason like &quot;Solars are the worst&quot; or &quot;We DB don't deserve to be at the bottom&quot;, they decided to do it because each of them had different cultural, personal, historical and political reasons to decide to destroy the Solars and Lunars. That's what I really like about 3e in general : I feel everything that happen is worth a story of its own, with its own determining factors. The DB and people of the Cha'Sca Empire and around rose against their God-Kings Champions because they desecrated their honors and broke the hierarchy among the clans they created themselves. The DB and people of the Ikir Kingdoms rose against their Solar Pharaos because they lied to them about destroying the 3rd Circle demon their ancestors brought down together. The DB and people of the now Blessed Isle rose against their Brotherhood because they used the Realm Defense Grid in a conflict that could be resolved through peace and diplomacy.<br /> <br /> The Sidereals could still have prepared for this moment (and encourage it), having the prisons and things ready to prevent Solars from reincarnating, but I for the moment I'm much more interested in seeing things like this than that &quot;World was led by Solars overlord with everyone else as their slave and they unanimously decided to kill them because they didn't like to live in slavery and were promised power by the Sidereals&quot; which I feel remove a lot of their individuality. I think a major success of Exalted 3e is that it makes you feel each culture is unique and worth trying to see the world through their eyes, so I like my perspective on these things because I think it goes along nicely with this feeling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":24291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","user":"Chausse","date":". 08-23-2020, 05:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-23T07:21:52-07:00","id":1409896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tikor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1409837#post1409837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Loved it. Facet Raven. Queen K'tula. That one time where every Exalt got to be the only Exalt in Creation because time broke and if they saved the world they got to re-merge with the prime timeline. The guidebook to Meru's dripping condescension for mortals. The art! The potential for drama!<br /> <br /> One of my players wishes to ascend to storyteller, and she is set on telling her story in the First Age. I can't think of higher praise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good luck to her. My experience is that the DotFA setting magnifies a lot of the problems people have with running Exalted.<br /> <br /> -The power disparity between the different Exalt types is underscored. <br /> - The absence of Abyssals and Infernals denies the ST an easy source of antagonism.<br /> - The abundance of NPCs who could probably fix the PCs problems that have nothing better to do.<br /> - The NPCs being too familiar to the PCs. Good luck trying to run Desus as the guy they slowly discover is an asshole. <br /> - The concept of Solars having their own Dragon-Blooded Gens can cause major focusing issues. <br /> - The leaning towards running a kingdom as a playstyle will bore the shit out of some players who were fine with it in vanilla but weren't prepared for how much they'd basically be sitting around saying &quot;hey, remember when we used to go on adventures?&quot;<br /> - The antipathy for mortals undermining the above for players who might otherwise be invested in it.<br /> <br /> Still, trial by fire works for a lot of people. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-23T09:54:05-07:00","id":1409923,"title":"","content":"My favorite part of the idea of 300 Solars somehow reducing 1M Dragon-Blooded to chattel is \u201cYou and what army?\u201d Those DBs <i>were</i> the army.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-23T12:26:00-07:00","id":1409945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1409923#post1409923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My favorite part of the idea of 300 Solars somehow reducing 1M Dragon-Blooded to chattel is \u201cYou and what army?\u201d Those DBs <i>were</i> the army.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. Hadn\u2019t thought about that. You raise a good point. But then how do you explain a whole gens of enslaved Dragon-Blooded sex workers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-23T13:01:22-07:00","id":1409955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1409923#post1409923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My favorite part of the idea of 300 Solars somehow reducing 1M Dragon-Blooded to chattel is \u201cYou and what army?\u201d Those DBs <i>were</i> the army.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the basic idea there is that a single Dawn can fairly easily slay 3,000-4,000 Dragonblooded warriors, see above where a Dawn can attack all enemies within 30 miles with accuracy and damage that splats anything without a perfect defense, for which the Dragonblooded ones explicitly fail against any form of Exalted magic.<br /> <br /> That wouldn't even be necessary, though, because a single Zenith could just use Horizon-to-Horizon Performance Method to target all Dragonblooded in a circle 2,000 miles wide with a social attack that annihilates their MDV and just convince them all to shut up and get on their knees, and they would do it. The Solar could even combine that with a charm that erases the memories of the Dragonblooded, and convinces them that there has never been any sort of discontent for the rule of the Solar in their whole life.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Which are both also reasons people said that the Usurpation couldn't happen, and examples of DotFA being utterly inconsistent with the game lore. Solars were given the mega epic high essence charms that allowed them to fight thousands of Dragonblooded and win easily, or dominate their minds and cast them into hell with nothing but a song. Then the Dragonblooded, who barely lived long enough to reach Essence 6 in the first place, were given a fraction of the charm count, and most of them, while cool, didn't help in the slightest when being matched against Solar power.<br /> <br /> So even the tiny handful of DB elders who did exist couldn't justify defending against Solar elders, and all the other DBs who were in the vast majority Essence 2-4 had no hope.<br /> <br /> Also Sidereals didn't even get new ability charms, just a new MA style, in case you were thinking the elder Sidereals must have done all the heavy lifting here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 08-23-2020, 04:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-23T13:05:33-07:00","id":1409956,"title":"","content":"I like much DotFA , I create a game much functional and the PCs, Solars and Sidereals with Essence 6 and 7, still having problems. The main PC's problem is avoid the Deliberative rules and fighting against the corrupted and mad celestial exalted. All characters from this game still &quot;living&quot; in the mind of my players and, often, they use then as part of a character's past or use in your games as plot device (many things leaved behind, like monsters and ruins).<br /> <br /> Sadly, the game don't go so long because of players agenda. I still have many notes, characters sheet and other things from this game, if anyone want, I can post a few things here. For me, DotFA is a very good and fun game, but need a dedicated GM to invest more energy to create a good and elaborated storyline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/437-shadowninja","name":"shadowninja","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-23T13:19:46-07:00","id":1409957,"title":"","content":"My impression of Dreams has changed over time, and I cannot repeat, with certainty, how I first felt about it.<br /> <br /> Currently, I view it as lazy.<br /> <br /> Not in the matter of the writing or production, which I know very little about, but in the world it depicts. The way the proliferation of artifacts is presented makes them cheap (not in the sense of cost to produce) out AND in setting. Significant aspects of the setting like the highly magitechnological armed forces seem like they were deliberately designed so that the Exalted didn't have to get involved. The Deliberative seems less like a governing body and more like an agreement for the young Exalts to not challenge the power and status of the entrenched powers in exchange for benefits. The Mandala Accords are almost literally written to give Exalts a moral pardon for being careless in their approach to the world/life.<br /> <br /> The setting has a deep fetishization of technology and the technological paradigm of the modern West, as if there is no other way that a sophisticated or prosperous or &quot;happy&quot; society could possibly be organized. There is almost no emphasis on personal cultivation of spiritual growth. Enlightenment can be accomplished with a medical procedure and is viewed more like a job certification than something life changing or personally transformative. Faith had gone from a fairly pragmatic, transactional orthopraxy to a cynical materialism on the level of paying your taxes. There is no sense of <i>respect</i> for anything, be it the gods or even the Exalted. All those sumptuary laws about things like who got to use what sidewalk point to a breakdown of respect and its replacement with mere law.<br /> <br /> The First Age of Dreams is late Numenor, at the noontide of its power but the gloaming of its wisdom and bliss. Its a world of people with the power to make life free and beautiful for everyone who just gave up on that project. It is tired and lost because it doesn't believe in anything to work toward other than increasing its own power and splendor forever as an end unto itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","user":"Exthalion","date":". 07-10-2023, 03:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-23T21:36:55-07:00","id":1410009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1409945#post1409945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm. Hadn\u2019t thought about that. You raise a good point. But then how do you explain a whole gens of enslaved Dragon-Blooded sex workers?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't. If something in a book contradicts, &quot;The Dragon-Blooded were the heroic soldiers and trusted bodyguards of the Exalted Host, as interesting and worthy of protagonist status as any other Exalt,&quot; I would cut that thing. Especially if that thing equates sex work to slavery, degradation, corruption, or some combination thereof.<br /> <br /> Might a gens gain a reputation for excellent sexual services? Sure. But that comes with a set of very human complications that would be interesting to explore without bringing magical slavery into the mix.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T03:54:19-07:00","id":1410033,"title":"","content":"The thing is DotFA doesn't really tell us shit about the Anjei, we're given Marama and left to work out what the situation actually is with the rest of the family. <br /> <br /> It could be that they've got a good clientele of prominently ranked Dragon-Blooded to exert soft power upon and siblings and cousins who once respected Marama now think she\u2019s actively embarrassing herself for chasing a new Celestial Exalt patronage. We don't know because space that could've been used to tell us more about the First Age as a playable setting was used to tell us what the future death camp commander was up to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T04:08:11-07:00","id":1410036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1410009#post1410009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't. If something in a book contradicts, &amp;quot;The Dragon-Blooded were the heroic soldiers and trusted bodyguards of the Exalted Host, as interesting and worthy of protagonist status as any other Exalt,&amp;quot; I would cut that thing. Especially if that thing equates sex work to slavery, degradation, corruption, or some combination thereof.<br /> <br /> Might a gens gain a reputation for excellent sexual services? Sure. But that comes with a set of very human complications that would be interesting to explore without bringing magical slavery into the mix.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like your second paragraph.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T18:53:40-07:00","id":1410179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1409338#post1409338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By reintroducing the Celestial Incarna as stated NPCs to be interact with rather than setting decoration it made the setting larger and more mythical. The charms in Glories, especially the Solar Charms are First Age charms and tell a story of their excess (accessing Abyssal charms, abusing the Solar Bond etc) while the ones in DotFA were just high essence.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the charms were superior in Glories, but I had the opposite reaction to the Incarna. I thought it was a horrible diminishing of their character and, in many ways, took them from multi-faceted myths down to near caricatures. Especially with the Unconquered Sun. His stats were not particularly fun, the errata'd version of him even less so, and the way they handled his background was such a hollowing out of his persona that I couldn't help but feel it was the culmination of everything I hated about very late 2nd edition.<br /> <br /> Of course, I actually still like Glories. It's Masters of Jade that made me go, &quot;Yup, I'm out.&quot; (It was just such an inferior product to Manacle &amp; Coin.) But that's not this topic.<br /> <br /> I'm going to back to lurking in the Scarred Lands room now.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13194-psyclus","name":"Psyclus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T21:14:41-07:00","id":1410213,"title":"","content":"Personally, as a fan of stuff that goes beyond the absolute impossible to truly mythic heights like Asura's Wrath, DBZ, Gurren Lagann, etc, I quite like how 2e went into the realms of truly mythically absurd by the end. Like, yeah, maybe it wasn't the healthiest for the game, but I still can't help but have a sort of unironic love for how DotFA's Solar Charms just utterly abandoned any pretense of balance and were borderline <i>cheating</i> in-universe to a level that would make most Japanese light novel heroes with <i>literal</i> cheat skills blush. Maybe it should not be done again, but shit, I am glad that canonically Exalted really did get that ridiculous at least once. Stuff like that Integrity charm that allows the Solar to still deal aggravated damage against CoD's even if the Unconquered Sun <i>fucking dies</i> (you know, the dude who literally defines what is a CoD to begin with) fills me with a cheesy dumbass grin.<br /> <br /> If I'd change anything I'd give the Lunars and Sidereals E5+ charms that extended into not quite as ridiculous, but still abnormally strong representations of their host Incarnae's themes. Closing the gap a little, if you will. Past E5, even the Lunars and Sids find themselves reaching heights their Incarnae never meant for them. Influence from Solars? Autochthon's intentional design? Who knows. The idea that humans exulted by the strongest of gods for being the most exemplary of humanity wouldn't <i>also </i>defy their original designs and stretch into realms of power never intended for them just because they weren't Gold is silly. <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">And the same goes for Dragon-blooded, yeah I'M ONE OF THOSE PEOPLE</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Exalted for me has always had that &quot;ROW ROW FIGHT THA POWAA&quot; feeling to it anyway. I am definitely one of those &quot;let's make EVERYONE OVERPOWERED AS HELL&quot; kind of people though so my opinion probably should be taken with a grain of salt. I understand that Exalted is meant to be a little different than that, but hey, that's what houseruling and headcanons are for.<br /> <br /> Things like the First Age being a super high-tech Science Fantasy world didn't bother me in the slightest because Science Fantasy is my favorite damn genre to begin with so I was all for that goodness to begin with. I'm not invested in the whole idea of artifacts being precious gems that have to remain special and rare so that didn't matter to me either. My issues with the 2e First Age were all with the writing of the actual characters, not the setting and themes themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4801,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","user":"Frostav","date":". 08-25-2020, 12:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","name":"Frostav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T21:46:38-07:00","id":1410217,"title":"","content":"Okay to clarify, I didn\u2019t agree with Glories <b>intended</b> purpose of making the Incarna relevant in the Age of Sorrow. I personally found that led to some jarring retcons of the basic setting.<br /> <br /> But a more accessible and Unconquered Sun for an alternative game setting that takes place before he turned his back on the world? That\u2019s cool, even if I\u2019m sure people would\u2019ve fucked it up somehow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T21:57:29-07:00","id":1410219,"title":"","content":"If I have one big criticism of DotFA, it's a personal thing I have with Exalted: I always thought the idea of exploring the Solars, people straight-up designed to beat the Primordials, struggling to self-actualize and fulfill themselves in a world where they have objectively Won Everything to be cool and DotFA barely touches on it. I'm more into the idea of Solars who just plain don't know what to do with their power and ambition because they've Done Everything they possibly can. Granted, they are canonically supposed to be rulers, but hell, when you have that much puissance and nothing new to do, something's gotta give eventually. What gives could make for a good story, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","name":"Frostav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T22:21:20-07:00","id":1410225,"title":"","content":"In terms of setting I think Dreams of the First Age is like reading a book on Quantum Physics. It's really pretty to cool at and mine for some ideas, but ultimately unusable for the vast majority of games. Putting aside the Magitech, what do you even do? Vanilla Exalted starts you off with a certain amount of power which then lets you earn the rest, but having First Age backgrounds makes that almost obsolete. It makes the First Age more interesting as a case study.<br /> <br /> The charm power (The errata'd one) are logical progressions and are mostly fine. Strange that the first release of DotFA had no Exalted charms in them. There's just empty space in my PDF. Strange.<br /> <br /> Despite all this, I think the Guidebook to Meru is not only my favorite first age book but also one of my favorite books of the line. It goes into detail on many of the high notes of the first age, with each being a proper length never to get to stale and to leave things fresh for exploring things further. It's also written in-universe, which I am an immediate sucker for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T23:05:03-07:00","id":1410234,"title":"","content":"Yeah. There's potential in the Dreams books but the actual writing squandered a lot of it.<br /> <br /> That said, I am <i>here</i> for a Shogunate setting because I feel like that lets you have a lot of the First Age 'feel' in some ways - the world has not yet had the second diminishment of the Great Contagion - but in a way a little more recognizable and <i>relevant</i> to an Age of Sorrows game.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T04:48:49-07:00","id":1410267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aliasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1410234#post1410234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. There's potential in the Dreams books but the actual writing squandered a lot of it.<br /> <br /> That said, I am <i>here</i> for a Shogunate setting because I feel like that lets you have a lot of the First Age 'feel' in some ways - the world has not yet had the second diminishment of the Great Contagion - but in a way a little more recognizable and <i>relevant</i> to an Age of Sorrows game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can\u2019t wait for the Shogunate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T14:21:27-07:00","id":1410394,"title":"","content":"I think with the current edition's focus on the today and living in the results of history, it'll be a while yet before we get snippets on the Shoguante I think. There was apparently a Shogunate book slated before 3e was put into development, but that's on a pretty significantly forked timeline at this point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-26T02:00:15-07:00","id":1410478,"title":"","content":"Isn\u2019t Heirs to the Shogunate about the Shogunate?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-26T02:11:16-07:00","id":1410483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1410478#post1410478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn\u2019t Heirs to the Shogunate about the Shogunate?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. It is about the Heirs. The various Dragon-blooded ruled dominions in the current setting.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-26T02:15:16-07:00","id":1410485,"title":"","content":"Ohhhh. Okay. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-26T03:28:42-07:00","id":1410489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1410225#post1410225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Strange that the first release of DotFA had no Exalted charms in them. There's just empty space in my PDF. Strange.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm still annoyed that there's no PDF with the original run of Charms in it available.<br /> <br /> I'd almost consider looking around for a physical book of the original print, but apart from the storage issues I expect such things would be expensive <i>and</i> of low structural quality.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-26T13:27:58-07:00","id":1410556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1410478#post1410478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn\u2019t Heirs to the Shogunate about the Shogunate?</div> </div> </div> </div>As noted it's about its modern heirs, not it itself. The Realm, Lookshy, and Prasad all claim to be inheritors of the Shoguante's legacy, kind of like how a lot of European powers claimed to be the inheritors of Rome's.<br /> <br /> Again, we're likely not going to get a historical book for this edition anytime soon at all, let alone one about htis time period beyond what books like DBs, Lunars, and Arms do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-27T06:46:53-07:00","id":1410671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1410489#post1410489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm still annoyed that there's no PDF with the original run of Charms in it available.<br /> <br /> I'd almost consider looking around for a physical book of the original print, but apart from the storage issues I expect such things would be expensive <i>and</i> of low structural quality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Most people who purchased the boxed set experienced the Time of Cascading Pages where the binding in Lands of Creation and Lords of Creation proved to be less than adequate.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-27T12:04:51-07:00","id":1410724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1410671#post1410671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. Most people who purchased the boxed set experienced the Time of Cascading Pages where the binding in Lands of Creation and Lords of Creation proved to be less than adequate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mine is still together but I fully admit it lives mostly in a box and it may ahve just aged out.<br /> <br /> Also remember how low res the map was. It actually was so bad that it made me hesitant on the 3e one until I found out that one was pretty nice canvas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-27T14:33:06-07:00","id":1410765,"title":"","content":"Hoo boy, am I conflicted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-27T14:39:36-07:00","id":1410767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1410765#post1410765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hoo boy, am I conflicted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Something along the lines of &quot;it was a worthy experiment that we learned a lot from, and Third Edition would not look like it does if we hadn't learned what we did from that attempt&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-28T00:23:28-07:00","id":1410810,"title":"","content":"The idea of Solar Exalted having to actualize and having to deal with the fact that there are no more fights to win is a nice one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-28T01:52:28-07:00","id":1410814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1410810#post1410810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea of Solar Exalted having to actualize and having to deal with the fact that there are no more fights to win is a nice one.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Maybe it's an interesting thing to read and talk about, but it seems like a terrible idea for a setting and characters to play an actual game in.<br /> <br /> Or at least a game running on this engine.<br /> <br /> As usual, the Dawn Caste seems to suffer the most from this. &quot;All right! I've effectively used these advanced character creation rules to construct a character who is plausibly beyond all martial challenges. Now to play out a chronicle of them grappling with the ennui of realising that there's nothing to do anymore and they're still not satisfied with life. That's exactly the kind of play experience I wanted out of a Dawn, right?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-28T02:42:35-07:00","id":1410816,"title":"","content":"I want to be a little positive, so maybe we could talk about First Age PCs?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-28T04:19:13-07:00","id":1410823,"title":"","content":"I wouldn\u2019t mind playing a Lunar if I ever played in a First Age campaign setting. Probably a No Moon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-28T05:54:51-07:00","id":1410836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1410814#post1410814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As usual, the Dawn Caste seems to suffer the most from this. &amp;quot;All right! I've effectively used these advanced character creation rules to construct a character who is plausibly beyond all martial challenges. Now to play out a chronicle of them grappling with the ennui of realising that there's nothing to do anymore and they're still not satisfied with life. That's exactly the kind of play experience I wanted out of a Dawn, right?&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s also not even true at all. There\u2019s 60 Dawns in the first age. It doesn\u2019t take a genius to figure out that it makes no sense to have 60 warriors so powerful that nobody in the universe may offer even an interesting battle. The solution to your problem is to go fight one of the other guys that\u2019s utterly invincible. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1410816#post1410816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to be a little positive, so maybe we could talk about First Age PCs?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well my group did a flashback session once where we were all people at the very end of the high first age, and we were asked by our ST to show off how awesome and terrible it was. I was the Dawn so I made a character who bombed around the Wyld in a massive airship that\u2019s launched combining warstriders, and who threw away lives like tissue paper in his search for ever greater glory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-28T14:56:49-07:00","id":1410889,"title":"","content":"Talking about Lunars, there *are* gripes there. I think Celestials should be group in all of their own, and that solars shouldn't just order them around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-28T18:29:55-07:00","id":1410915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1410889#post1410889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Talking about Lunars, there *are* gripes there. I think Celestials should be group in all of their own, and that solars shouldn't just order them around.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. The Solar-Lunar soulmate bond needs to be more a relationship of equals. Maybe they\u2019ll do that in Fangs at the Gate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-28T19:32:54-07:00","id":1410922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1410915#post1410915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree. The Solar-Lunar soulmate bond needs to be more a relationship of equals. Maybe they\u2019ll do that in Fangs at the Gate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup. Like, I&quot;m now reading: <br /> <br /> &quot;Banished him to the rural principalities, where he takes out his frustratiosn on the natives.&quot; <br /> <br /> Girl, you just banished your lunar mate to somewhere else. Like a lapdog. Bitch, that's a celestial level exalted that can tear a mortal apart limb to limb.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-28T21:27:27-07:00","id":1410945,"title":"","content":"I loved the setting book, and I still have the map up on my wall. Every page of that book was &quot;oh this is why the First Age ended. Oh no THIS is why...&quot; <br /> <br /> The system book was bad. There were a few good ideas, but the execution was... Let's say that a lot of people didn't realize how 2e charms and rules worked. And there were entire pages just devoted to NPC charm lists. What a waste.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Current project: <a href=\"https://monsterambulance.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Monster Ambulance</a>, wherein you save monsters. In your ambulance.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2240-colin_fredericks","name":"Colin_Fredericks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2240_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-28T22:48:25-07:00","id":1410951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colin_Fredericks</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1410945#post1410945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I loved the setting book, and I still have the map up on my wall. Every page of that book was &quot;oh this is why the First Age ended. Oh no THIS is why...&quot;<br /> <br /> The system book was bad. There were a few good ideas, but the execution was... Let's say that a lot of people didn't realize how 2e charms and rules worked. And there were entire pages just devoted to NPC charm lists. What a waste.</div> </div> </div> </div>They should have just said: &quot;Ok, she has all socialize and performance charms that reach Essence 5, and this this this essence 6/7/8 charm....&quot; instead of giant lists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-28T23:20:55-07:00","id":1410953,"title":"","content":"Can't! <i>*clap*</i> Wait! <i>*clap*</i> For the Sho! Gun! Ate! <i>*clap clap clap*</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-29T00:04:31-07:00","id":1410958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1410915#post1410915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe they\u2019ll do that in Fangs at the Gate.</div> </div> </div> </div>They did, past tense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-29T03:59:27-07:00","id":1410981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1410958#post1410958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They did, past tense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool. Idk that cause I didn\u2019t back the Kickstarter. I\u2019ll buy it when it comes out on DTRPG.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-29T07:18:42-07:00","id":1410992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1410889#post1410889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Talking about Lunars, there *are* gripes there. I think Celestials should be group in all of their own, and that solars shouldn't just order them around.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think in the context of DotFA's setting the inequality itself is was a problem but rather how it was used.<br /> Lilith and Ma-Ha-Suchi dominate the discourse when talking about Lunars in this supplement but Ingosh Silverclaws and Tamuz were <b>way</b> more interesting because they highlight the tension between near equals.<br /> <br /> One of the DotFA games I played in had a subplot about Lunars pushing for political reform it was an altered timeline after a second Aftershock War and a lot of the Solar elders who'd stymied their ambitions were now dead so their power grab had a very real chance of success.<br /> <br /> Another had the Lunars and Sidereals masterminding the Usurpation to form the Night Sky Regime which somehow managed to capture the tone of Tron Uprising years before that show aired.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-29T13:18:51-07:00","id":1411020,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7\" data-vbnamecard=\"7\">Lioness</a> are Lilith and Tammuz intended to reflect their counterparts from RL myth? If so, is this still true in Fangs at the Gate?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-29T23:53:16-07:00","id":1411049,"title":"","content":"Nothing I\u2019ve ever heard about 2e Lilith is anything like her namesake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-30T00:52:06-07:00","id":1411052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1411020#post1411020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7\" data-vbnamecard=\"7\">Lioness</a> are Lilith and Tammuz intended to reflect their counterparts from RL myth? If so, is this still true in Fangs at the Gate?</div> </div> </div> </div>Lilith if anything draws most on the World of Darkness Lilith in that she is an ancient owl-related being who is linked to a young naive powerful person (Swan). I think the parallel intially was supposed to be her-to-Swan had elements of Lilith-to-Caine from <b>Vampire: the Masquerade</b> but it went completely off that tract probably before <b>Exalted</b> ever was published.<br /> <br /> Tammuz has like, nothing ot do with his mythological namesake. He originallyw as just a name of a Lunar who was less violently anti-civlization in the 1e Lunars book and there's little to nothing of him I think that draws on anything about Sumerian mythologys ave being int eh vaguely Middle Eastern-inspired region of near CHiaroscuro.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-30T07:33:48-07:00","id":1411071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1411020#post1411020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7\" data-vbnamecard=\"7\">Lioness</a> are Lilith and Tammuz intended to reflect their counterparts from RL myth? If so, is this still true in Fangs at the Gate?</div> </div> </div> </div>Like Blaque says. If mythology is being invoked it's either a really deep dive or they're based primarily on other fictionalised versions of these characters to the extent they no longer resemble the source material. <br /> <br /> Tamuz is not in Fangs at the Gate, my understanding is that he's been given the Schr\u00f6dinger's Cat treatment. Where he probably won't appear in 3rd edition officially for the sake of keeping the canonical number of First Age Lunars down but if he's still part of your game's lore then nothing breaks. Honestly, a First Age Lunar as the secret patron of the Delzhan whose spent centuries operating under the nose of the Realm might actually work better if it's not documented in a major source book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-30T09:45:45-07:00","id":1411083,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7\" data-vbnamecard=\"7\">Lioness</a> thank you.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar353_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"353\" data-vbnamecard=\"353\">Blaque</a> who\u2019s Swan? Her abusive husband\u2019s name in DotFA was Desus. Makes me think of a romance between Lilith and Lohengrin the Swan Knight (I took a class on medieval romances one time).<br /> <br /> REALLY looking forward to finally reading Fangs at the Gate. I wasn\u2019t that into Exalted back then or I would\u2019ve backed the Kickstarter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25665,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 08-30-2020, 12:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-30T10:09:41-07:00","id":1411086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1411083#post1411083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">who\u2019s Swan?</div> </div> </div> </div>Swan's a signature character from previous editions, an Eclipse sailor and diplomat who took his Second Breath after the Jade Prison was broken open. He's also the inheritor of the bond to Lilith. In 1e this meant things were... complicated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-30T10:12:16-07:00","id":1411087,"title":"","content":"Swan was the signature Eclipse Caste of 1st and 2nd edition and Desus' canonical reincarnation, thus making him Lilith's new mate.<br /> <br /> This is why if I'd somehow been responsible for Fangs at the Gate I'd have cut Lilith, since by connecting her to Swan she'd never seemed like a full fledged character so much as inspiration that a PC's First Age spouse might still be alive and not necessarily pleased to see them again. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-30T16:45:26-07:00","id":1411133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1411052#post1411052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lilith if anything draws most on the World of Darkness Lilith in that she is an ancient owl-related being who is linked to a young naive powerful person (Swan). I think the parallel intially was supposed to be her-to-Swan had elements of Lilith-to-Caine from <b>Vampire: the Masquerade</b> but it went completely off that tract probably before <b>Exalted</b> ever was published.<br /> <br /> Tammuz has like, nothing ot do with his mythological namesake. He originallyw as just a name of a Lunar who was less violently anti-civlization in the 1e Lunars book and there's little to nothing of him I think that draws on anything about Sumerian mythologys ave being int eh vaguely Middle Eastern-inspired region of near CHiaroscuro.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tamuz was also distinct from Tomas Khan, the Lunar who was big into the Delzahn. Then 2e conflated them, to terrible, terrible results.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-30T17:53:38-07:00","id":1411140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1411087#post1411087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">by connecting her to Swan she'd never seemed like a full fledged character so much as inspiration that a PC's First Age spouse might still be alive and not necessarily pleased to see them again. </div> </div> </div> </div>It seems to me like First Edition had a thing where write-ups for important characters would reference things in chapter fictions, but leave the names out.<br /> <br /> So those pieces might have an ongoing narrative including Ma-Ha-Suchi fighting Dace, but the identity of who fought the old goat in canon is otherwise open-ended.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1411133#post1411133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Tamuz was also distinct from Tomas Khan, the Lunar who was big into the Delzahn. Then 2e conflated them, to terrible, terrible results.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know about this Tomas Khan, but I distinctly recall from reading Exalted: the Lunars a year ago that it draws a connection between Tammuz and the Delzhan, including him having a role in their initial conquest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-30T21:33:19-07:00","id":1411165,"title":"","content":"Interesting<br /> <br /> Like I said, I\u2019m really looking forward to seeing what they do with Fangs at the Gate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-31T05:49:35-07:00","id":1411201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1411140#post1411140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems to me like First Edition had a thing where write-ups for important characters would reference things in chapter fictions, but leave the names out.<br /> <br /> So those pieces might have an ongoing narrative including Ma-Ha-Suchi fighting Dace, but the identity of who fought the old goat in canon is otherwise open-ended.</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't feel it was very effective at empowering players and storytellers to feel that they could cultivate alternative stories around those things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-31T13:20:43-07:00","id":1411238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1411140#post1411140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know about this Tomas Khan, but I distinctly recall from reading Exalted: the Lunars a year ago that it draws a connection between Tammuz and the Delzhan, including him having a role in their initial conquest.</div> </div> </div> </div>I misspelled Tamas Khan, but otherwise, check page 41, second to last paragraph before the Jackal Tribe entry. In contrast, Tamuz was said to have recruited from everywhere but the Jackal Tribes, and if the Delzahn were intended on being a part of his schtick, then his writeup is curiously empty of any stated connection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-01T18:01:08-07:00","id":1411448,"title":"","content":"I liked dreams--but I think it was a case of showing that the rules system really, really wasn't set up to handle high-level essence games. <br /> <br /> Personally, I've been thinking of redoing it with 3E rules, while keeping the magitech focus. <br /> (I really miss the magitech in exalted.).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-02T00:40:37-07:00","id":1411482,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I find the Realm presented in Lands of Creation to already not nearly be so magitech heavy as one might expect, or as many people seem to recall or desire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-02T06:03:28-07:00","id":1411497,"title":"","content":"What about I AM? Like a magical Internet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-02T15:26:46-07:00","id":1411576,"title":"","content":"This is an incredibly minor thing but I love this bit from a Solar Survival charm DotFA:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> She<br /> places representations the five elements at the center and<br /> directional boundaries of the shelter (these representations<br /> can be actual examples of each element, such as twigs, stone,<br /> cinders, etc, or the Solar may use a few drops of blood, paper<br /> effigies, <b>Dragon-Blooded willing to sit still</b>, or other tokens) </div> </div> </div>Ah, Exalted. I love when it gets a teensy bit whimsically silly like this in the middle of extremely ornate and mythic prose. I especially like how it showcases the intended (in-universe) relationship between Solars and DB's without just trashing the latter and making them out to be worthless cannon fodder/slaves/bad things like so much of 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4801,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","user":"Frostav","date":". 09-02-2020, 06:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","name":"Frostav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T01:00:21-07:00","id":1411614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1411497#post1411497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about I AM? Like a magical Internet.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is precisely the problem. IAM is practically a prosthetic primordial, a mind of pure essence interwoven with the world whose fractal selves continuously split and reform, charged with the preservation of all the splendors of the Solar Realm and all that dwelt therein. A pantheon in one who was both friend and servant to might and mortal alike.<br /> <br /> And they made it the internet. They stripped out all the grandure and gravitas to leave the most banal possible presentation. As if a synod of superhumans with the blessings of the gods and the unrivaled dominion couldn't do better than us comfortable 20th century humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T02:18:59-07:00","id":1411622,"title":"","content":"Huh. Idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T02:20:52-07:00","id":1411623,"title":"","content":"Huh. I have an idea. How about I Am doesn't just have terminals. He's everywhere. You know how some people say reality is composed out of code and thst code can be manipulated? That's I Am. At low levels he can work with sidereals to reduce fate disruptions and seal off damages to reality like fair folk incursions. At higher levels, the laws of physics are under his command.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T07:13:59-07:00","id":1411636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1411576#post1411576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">without just trashing the latter and making them out to be worthless cannon fodder/slaves/bad things like so much of 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>...It specifically puts them on the same level as random detritus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T08:44:39-07:00","id":1411646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1411614#post1411614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And they made it the internet. They stripped out all the grandure and gravitas to leave the most banal possible presentation. As if a synod of superhumans with the blessings of the gods and the unrivaled dominion couldn't do better than us comfortable 20th century humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bIAM is one of those things where what's actually in the books doesn't look that bad but almost immediately after the boxed set came out people were treating it exactly like the internet with web pages etc (I was guilty of this too) rather than an artificial sentience that\u2019s capable of holding ten thousand, trillion, trillion, trillion, trillion, trillion *deep breath* trillion, trillion, trillion conversations at once.<br /> <br /> As such it seems unlikely that it\u2019d facilitate a set-up of Solars cultivating social media profiles and sharing memes when its probably more like the magic mirror in Snow White telling the evil queen she's beautiful as a form of harm reduction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T12:32:39-07:00","id":1411673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1411636#post1411636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...It specifically puts them on the same level as random detritus.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a joke.<br /> <br /> That's like the most negative interpretation possible. To me it gave off the very funny impression of a Solar telling five dragon-blooded to sit and meditate in a circle. If the charm requires manifestations of the elements, why <i>wouldn't</i> it allow dragon-blooded to substitute them?<br /> <br /> Like damn, man. It's a funny joke. Humor. Like the part of the Sid book where it says &quot;Young sidereals are advised not to eat their operational budgets&quot; or the infamous cake art/story. You are taking an amusing line <i>way</i> too seriously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4801,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","user":"Frostav","date":". 09-03-2020, 03:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","name":"Frostav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T12:40:42-07:00","id":1411678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1411646#post1411646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bIAM is one of those things where what's actually in the books doesn't look that bad but almost immediately after the boxed set came out people were treating it exactly like the internet with web pages etc (I was guilty of this too) rather than an artificial sentience that\u2019s capable of holding ten thousand, trillion, trillion, trillion, trillion, trillion *deep breath* trillion, trillion, trillion conversations at once.<br /> <br /> As such it seems unlikely that it\u2019d facilitate a set-up of Solars cultivating social media profiles and sharing memes when its probably more like the magic mirror in Snow White telling the evil queen she's beautiful as a form of harm reduction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why couldn\u2019t I AM be both? A social media network for the general public and a magic mirror for the Exalted elite?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4801\" data-vbnamecard=\"4801\">Frostav</a> what\u2019s the cake art/story?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T12:55:07-07:00","id":1411680,"title":"","content":"That one of a Twilight's Lunar Mate eating all of the cakes she made for an occasion. It was a 2e comic (can't remember which one) and was a chapter fiction in 3e's corebook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","name":"Frostav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T13:44:56-07:00","id":1411687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1411680#post1411680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That one of a Twilight's Lunar Mate eating all of the cakes she made for an occasion. It was a 2e comic (can't remember which one) and was a chapter fiction in 3e's corebook.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was a single art piece in Masters of Jade, where the Lunar was unconcerned with concealing herself, and an alternate single piece in the EX3 core, where the Lunar is sneaking away from a Solar who doesn't know what the hell happened. Only in MoJ is the incident explained in context (an attempt to disrupt the Solar baker's burgeoning business relationship with the Guild).<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">Lunars eating cake - serious business.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T13:56:42-07:00","id":1411691,"title":"","content":"Awesome!!! Imma tell my BFF that. Her mom owns a cake shop.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25665,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 09-03-2020, 09:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T15:22:15-07:00","id":1411709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1411614#post1411614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is precisely the problem. IAM is practically a prosthetic primordial, a mind of pure essence interwoven with the world whose fractal selves continuously split and reform, charged with the preservation of all the splendors of the Solar Realm and all that dwelt therein. A pantheon in one who was both friend and servant to might and mortal alike.<br /> <br /> And they made it the internet. They stripped out all the grandure and gravitas to leave the most banal possible presentation. As if a synod of superhumans with the blessings of the gods and the unrivaled dominion couldn't do better than us comfortable 20th century humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>We are forced to try and develop relationships with one another. As I recall, people at the tail end of the First Age were largely forming highly personalised relationships with I AM. That's a level of precision much beyond what is currently possible, and carries a fair number of implications.<br /> <br /> Still, I'll be interested if Lea sees this and has an interesting response to this critique of his work. I recall when he described submitting I AM and it upping the game on the book's writing a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T16:24:27-07:00","id":1411715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1411673#post1411673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's like the most negative interpretation possible. To me it gave off the very funny impression of a Solar telling five dragon-blooded to sit and meditate in a circle. If the charm requires manifestations of the elements, why <i>wouldn't</i> it allow dragon-blooded to substitute them?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's pretty amusing, but also definitely paints the Dragonblooded as trash. The Solar could use a drop of blood, a twig, scrub of grass, or a paper effigy of a tree, but instead he's ordering an Exalted servant to sit down and shut up for an hour because their body is an acceptable token for wood essence. That's like needing a footstool and ordering his Exalted retainer to get down on all fours so he can put his boots on their back.<br /> <br /> It's the kind of action that could, and did, help drive somebody to smash their Solar liege's skull in with a goremaul at Calibration dinner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T16:45:02-07:00","id":1411716,"title":"","content":"Correction: It\u2019s like <i>having</i> a footstool but using your Exalted retainer as one instead because there\u2019s clearly nothing more useful they could be doing anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T16:53:21-07:00","id":1411718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1411716#post1411716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Correction: It\u2019s like <i>having</i> a footstool but using your Exalted retainer as one instead because there\u2019s clearly nothing more useful they could be doing anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>V'neef was the Scarlet Empress' cupbearer.<br /> <br /> If a person can perform double duty as the individual who pours your drinks, laces up your shoes or helps you get dressed in the morning and being a second in command who wields extraordinary power on your behalf, or in the course of attending to you during official business can be groomed for their own leadership, I see no reason why participating in some spell or Charm should be any different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T17:12:36-07:00","id":1411721,"title":"","content":"There\u2019s a difference between being someone\u2019s cupbearer and being their cupholder. We\u2019re discussing a joke that\u2019s explicitly about treating a Dragon-Blooded as interchangeable with an inanimate object. The kind you can find lying on the ground no less.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T17:31:31-07:00","id":1411722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1411718#post1411718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a person can perform double duty as the individual who pours your drinks, laces up your shoes or helps you get dressed in the morning and being a second in command who wields extraordinary power on your behalf, or in the course of attending to you during official business can be groomed for their own leadership, I see no reason why participating in some spell or Charm should be any different.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the spell required that it be something like &quot;A shard from the pure heart of each elemental pole, or a dragonblood of the same element&quot; then the DB in question is standing there in place of a precious object that may take weeks or months to get. Instead the DB is standing there because the Solar couldn't be bothered to prick their finger, or grab a tuft of grass, or wood-hafted tool/weapon.<br /> <br /> It could <i>theoretically </i>be a position of honour, like only the greatest and most noble exalted get to stand in that position, and in doing so they automatically earn enormous political clout, but there's absolutely nothing that suggests that was the case. In fact I feel like the wording is more akin to something you'd say about a dog or a child, which is part of the joke. You're talking about a person like they're a dog, and using them in place of a piece of random trash you could find laying about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T18:06:34-07:00","id":1411724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1411721#post1411721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There\u2019s a difference between being someone\u2019s cupbearer and being their cupholder.</div> </div> </div> </div>Insofar as the former term denotes that the person who hands your cup to you and fills it at your gesture is a position of great respect, sure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">treating a Dragon-Blooded as interchangeable with an inanimate object. The kind you can find lying on the ground no less.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Mercedes-Benz is interchangeable for any old banger for the purposes of getting you around. A valet who follows you about to hold up an umbrella is interchangeable with your hand.<br /> <br /> Those are differences not of practicality, but of prestige.<br /> <br /> If it's beneath the dignity of the Dragon Blooded to ever be anybody's servant, I suppose the Razor and the Coin and the Magistrates are right out.<br /> <br /> I'm genuinely curious why I didn't see this degree of hangup over the group of outcastes dedicated to the purpose of performing highly strenuous worship rituals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T18:14:49-07:00","id":1411728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1411722#post1411722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Instead the DB is standing there because the Solar couldn't be bothered to prick their finger, or grab a tuft of grass, or wood-hafted tool/weapon.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds to me like it's the wrong way around; that the Solar who goes the cheap route of using any rubbish lying around couldn't be bothered to go to the efforts of employing some more grand elemental signifier. You phrase it like that, and it sounds as though you are the one bringing in the assumption that it's trivial to make Terrestrials stand around like that; the quotation itself implies that it is not.<br /> <br /> Sure it's flippant. That's not something anybody needs to flip their lid over.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dr Love Monkey</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It could <i>theoretically </i>be a position of honour, like only the greatest and most noble exalted get to stand in that position, and in doing so they automatically earn enormous political clout, but there's absolutely nothing that suggests that was the case. In fact I feel like the wording is more akin to something you'd say about a dog or a child, which is part of the joke. You're talking about a person like they're a dog, and using them in place of a piece of random trash you could find laying about.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's something you feel like, it seems to me that it's merely a matter of different priorities in what we expand the text into representing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T18:24:31-07:00","id":1411730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1411724#post1411724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Mercedes-Benz is interchangeable for any old banger for the purposes of getting you around. A valet who follows you about to hold up an umbrella is interchangeable with your hand.<br /> <br /> Those are differences not of practicality, but of prestige.</div> </div> </div> </div>A valet who holds your umbrella does it so you don't have to, they're doing something for you. The DB standing in for a twig isn't doing something for you, you just grabbed them instead of a twig. It's like having a valet jam their hand in the door to keep it wedged open so you can let the breeze in. It's not a valet answering the door, or doing anything that a random paperweight couldn't do. It is nothing even remotely like being a spiritual guide, military officer, or arbiter of the law and will of the empress.<br /> <br /> Then add onto that the fact that this valet is also an exalt, not just a mortal, but a being of prodigious supernatural power. You can make the case that it is a prestige thing, but that prestige is in showing off to other Solars. They use twigs and stones, you use exalts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T18:24:44-07:00","id":1411731,"title":"","content":"A cupbearer was cherished and honored in Ancient Greece and Rome<br /> <br /> Also, the Scarlet Empress was Dragon-Blooded just like the rest of the Imperial Dynasty. She was one of them. Very different than the unequal relationship between the Solars and their servants in the First Age.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T19:51:21-07:00","id":1411736,"title":"","content":"Man y'all i just thought it was amusing.<br /> <br /> I think a good solution is that the charm--which mind you makes a stable zone of Creation even in <i>the middle of hell</i>--instead of requiring merely random crap, <i>requires</i> some very strong manifestations of the elements, such as hearthstones from manses of the elements, or maybe huge jade tablets or obelisks. Then using DB's wouldn't feel like insulting them and more just &quot;hey, they <i>technically count</i> as manifestations of the elements!&quot;<br /> <br /> I will not let the amusing image of a Solar telling his DB friend to sit in a circle with some jade because he only has jade of the other four elements so he can make a zone of Creation in hell die, dammit. I'm sorry that's just way too amusing of idea, thinking of the DB rolling her eyes and sitting still while the Solar does his Solar Things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4801,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","user":"Frostav","date":". 09-03-2020, 10:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","name":"Frostav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T21:22:05-07:00","id":1411744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1411736#post1411736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will not let the amusing image of a Solar telling his DB friend to sit in a circle with some jade because he only has jade of the other four elements so he can make a zone of Creation in hell die, dammit. I'm sorry that's just way too amusing of idea, thinking of the DB rolling her eyes and sitting still while the Solar does his Solar Things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, I'm totally with you there, you're thinking something like a chummy pair of Solar/Terrestrials out and about trying to set up something, and for some reason he just can't start a fire in spite of being Essence 5 and Survival 5, but he's got his fire aspect buddy with him. Who could also set a fire but for whatever reason he just wants to use him instead, and god damnit if he'd just stop fidgeting for a few more minutes the charm would be done, dangit!<br /> <br /> That's not really the world of Dreams of the First Age. Dragonblooded are sworn to servitude to the Solar exalted before they're even born, don't even have a seat in the ruling government, and the Solars are reaching for insane heights of arrogance and lack of empathy. They're genetically altering people so their screams come out as musical notes, and then torturing groups of them in place of an orchestra. Then when they get bored of playing them, rather than get regular instruments, they build automations to continue the torture. They could make robots to play instruments, but they simply care so little that the smallest whim nudged them to make torture robots instead.<br /> <br /> Against that backdrop, the charm feels a lot less &quot;Ayyy buddy! Just sit over there for a bit, I dunno, read a book or something, I need some fire and you weren't doing anything anyway.&quot; and more &quot;Hmm, I need fire. You. Sit in this spot until I'm done. Why would I use ashes? You're a perfectly useful representation of fire. Question me like that again and you'll die before we get back to Creation.&quot; Hence the whole mass murder thing that's in the near future of DotFA.<br /> <br /> <br /> Not that it couldn't ever happen, there were some young Solars who weren't totally detached from humanity, but they were the minority and not often talked about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T00:03:24-07:00","id":1411749,"title":"","content":"That passage describing I AM at the beginning of Chapter 1 of <i>Lands of Creation</i> was something I wrote at the beginning of the Dreams of the First Age brainstorming process, in a big email chain between all the writers.<br /> <br /> There's a trick old White Wolf games used to pull when doing historic settings: Make the historic setting completely unlike what you were expecting based on the game it's an historic setting for. For example, <i><s>Aeon</s></i> Trinity was a post-post-apocalyptic sci-fi story about psychic metahumans, called Psions, engaging in diplomacy, rebuilding efforts, first contact with aliens, and military action in a solar system populated by a human diaspora following a disastrous war between a previous generation of much, <i>much</i> more powerful physical metahuman mutants called Aberrants who wrecked civilization. White Wolf announced the next game in the series would be called Aberrant and would be a prequel to that. &quot;Holy shit,&quot; everyone said, &quot;It's gonna be an apocalypse game set during the Aberrant war!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Surprise!&quot; said Aberrant, when it finally came out. &quot;I'm a fucking superhero game! Before Aberrants were civilization-wrecking mutants, they were superheroes straight out of Wildstorm comics!&quot; (Specifically the Wildstorm comics. Not really Marvel or DC.)<br /> <br /> And then White Wolf didn't even say what the next game in the series was gonna be called, just that it was gonna be another prequel, and people were like &quot;Uhhh... I bet it's gonna be called Aegis, that makes sense, it starts with an A, what'll it be about?&quot; and it was called Adventure! and was about the Shadow and the Rocketeer. Nobody saw that coming.<br /> <br /> I thought it would be very cool to do that with Exalted. There'd always been hints that the First Age was not really a high-fantasy setting as such, with Geoff describing the archetypal Lunar adventure as &quot;Barbarians fighting mutants in the ruins of a First Age shopping mall,&quot; art in the Solar castebooks showing peasants with washers and dryers, etc. So there was a chance the First Age game would be an ancient high fantasy thing, mostly the same as the Second Age but with everything moved up, oh, let's say two Essence dots and more available artifacts for everyone and the Solars not being hunted. And there was a chance the First Age would be a psudeo-Exalted-modern thing.<br /> <br /> And I kinda went &quot;Those both sound boring&quot; and spent a feverish evening going for a long walk and drinking a can of Jolt (Jolt still existed back then) and writing a short fiction piece about the Exalted of the First Age inventing God and using Him as the Internet, and then I lobbed that short fiction piece into the brainstorming email thread like a bomb in the hope of exploding the other writers' heads. This worked! The first reply I got was John Fucking Snead, <i>inventor of the Heptagram</i>, going &quot;Okay, I just wrote a couple of thousand words and now I need to throw them out, goddamn it Lea.&quot; To be clear, that was absolutely 100% my intent with I AM. The Exalted invented God, and are using him as the Internet, and that's just one example of the sort of fucking crazy bullshit the First Age was filled with. That it shouldn't be Exalted Modern, and that it shouldn't be basically normal Exalted with different politics, but that it should be high gonzo transhumanist cyberpunk world with millions of Dragon-Blooded and where the Celestial Exalted are each richer and more powerful than the wealthiest billionaire on Earth.<br /> <br /> And then I wrote a timeline and filled it with all the sorts of things I thought would absolutely have to go into a First Age timeline, including a second Primordial War and a civil war between the Exalted that legit destroyed Creation, but then became a relatively unimportant historical footnote because they're the Exalted and if they destroy Creation they can fucking fix it. More bigger grander weirder.<br /> <br /> And then we brainstormed Operation Wyldhand, which was meant to be the moment where the First Age had ceased to be teetering on the edge of collapse and had, clearly and officially, started its irreversible fall, and it had happened just recently enough that the setting at the point of the fall where you can feel it in your stomach and you're wheeling your arms in the hope that you can still catch your balance if you just just spin them hard enough even though another part of you knows that no, it's too late, you're going all the way down the stairs now.<br /> <br /> (I warned you about stairs.)<br /> <br /> In retrospect none of this was a good idea because a) there wasn't enough space in a single boxed set consisting of two softcovers and a chapbook (<i>Guide to Meru</i> is somewhat akin to the old World of Darkness &quot;chapbooks&quot; like <i>The Book of Nod</i>) to give fiction and mechanical support for a setting of the scope and complexity I was hoping to inspire in the other writers, and b) I'm not Jewish so doing anything with any variation of I AM THAT I AM is probably insensitive. Especially writing Him as a cross between the Internet and Gamera. <i>Nowadays</i>, I advocate for the version of the First Age that's like a high fantasy thing where it's may be two Essence dots higher than the Second Age and with different politics. But this is purely and only because I've become a coward in my old age.<br /> <br /> I hope this post helps to contextualize my previous comment, &quot;Hoo boy, am I conflicted.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":229,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","user":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","date":". 09-04-2020, 03:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T00:22:13-07:00","id":1411750,"title":"","content":"God, I miss being that guy. I miss being able to write like two hundred words so weird and exciting and appealing that they derailed the plans of other, much more experience writers and changed the course of a boxed set and Exalted history. I'm still not sure how to reconcile that with the certain knowledge, in retrospect, that it was a bad thing to do that made everything worse. Like, should I have not tried?<br /> <br /> Also, funfact: I pitched for a writing job on Dreams of the First Age not because I thought I had any good ideas, or even because I was excited by the prospect of working on it, but because back then I was still committed to collecting every Exalted book and thought it'd be easier to get ahold of this one if I wrote for it and got a comp copy than if I had to buy it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":229,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","user":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","date":". 09-04-2020, 03:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T01:20:56-07:00","id":1411754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1411576#post1411576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>She</i><br /> <i>places representations the five elements at the center and</i><br /> <i>directional boundaries of the shelter (these representations</i><br /> <i>can be actual examples of each element, such as twigs, stone,</i><br /> <i>cinders, etc, or the Solar may use a few drops of blood, paper</i><br /> <i>effigies, </i><b>Dragon-Blooded willing to sit still</b><i>, or other tokens) </i></div> </div> </div> </div>I get what you mean by a joke. It looks like it's written by Terry Pratchett explaining how the dwarves in \u00dcberwald handle trash, making a list of trash that dwarves produces &quot;used pickaxe, worthless rocks&quot; and adding a casual &quot;Troll brains&quot; to remind everyone that dwarves hates trolls and view them as lesser beings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T01:59:42-07:00","id":1411763,"title":"","content":"Interesting to see the process. IAM always seemed a bit to me like, &quot;Well, of course the First Age would have omnipresent AI? They've alluded to it already with Icemind and Eyem&quot;. As for calling the thing IAM, it seems like a logical extrapolation of Eyem plus a playful allusion to self-awareness and Descartes (&quot;I think therefore I am&quot;).<br /> <br /> (As to the Biblical dimension, well, anime and sci-fi tends to steal compulsively from Kabbalah and Catholic theology and such - Zohar Modifider, Plane of Briah, Yesod, Lance of Longinus, Deus, Atsiluth Eternal. And I look upon this and saw that it was good. Though in Exalted's world the allusions should probably be fairly more subtle than most to maintain mood and tone).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T02:31:32-07:00","id":1411765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1411678#post1411678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why couldn\u2019t I AM be both? A social media network for the general public and a magic mirror for the Exalted elite?</div> </div> </div> </div>A social media network reduces I AM to something primitive for the sake of an easy reference and ignores the fact it has wildly different origins to the modern internet.<br /> <br /> Details on websites also have the potential to age like milk and end up as a potentially cringe inducing collection of dated references before the edition is over.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T06:53:23-07:00","id":1411781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> She places representations the five elements at the center and directional boundaries of the shelter (these representations can be actual examples of each element, such as twigs, stone, cinders, etc, or the Solar may use a few drops of blood, paper effigies, <b>Dragon-Blooded willing to sit still</b>, or other tokens) </div> </div> </div>Out of context, I interpreted that as<i> &quot;it <b>would</b> work, but good luck convincing an Exalted to act as your twigs and stones!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Kind of like if you had a ritual that went &quot;you may use a lamp, a torch, a cooperative Unconquered Sun, or other sources of light&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T06:55:22-07:00","id":1411782,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar229_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"229\" data-vbnamecard=\"229\">Stephen Lea Sheppard</a> awesome!!! I loved DotFA. Got me into Exalted.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4801\" data-vbnamecard=\"4801\">Frostav</a> I thought it was funny \ud83d\ude0a. Not everything has to be all grimdark.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7\" data-vbnamecard=\"7\">Lioness</a> hmm, good points","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T07:16:43-07:00","id":1411793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1411736#post1411736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man y'all i just thought it was amusing.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s <i>very</i> amusing. Just, you know, in a way that <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1411754#post1411754\">Chausse already described best</a>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1411749#post1411749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In retrospect none of this was a good idea because a) there wasn't enough space in a single boxed set consisting of two softcovers and a chapbook (Guide to Meru is somewhat akin to the old World of Darkness &quot;chapbooks&quot; like The Book of Nod) to give fiction and mechanical support for a setting of the scope and complexity I was hoping to inspire in the other writers, and b) I'm not Jewish so doing anything with any variation of I AM THAT I AM is probably insensitive.</div> </div> </div> </div>My brain, immediately: \u201cLimitations that Storyteller\u2019s Vault and I respectively do not have.\u201d<br /> <br /> <i>Now look what you\u2019ve done.</i> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T09:05:00-07:00","id":1411807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1411749#post1411749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I hope this post helps to contextualize my previous comment, &quot;Hoo boy, am I conflicted.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that a lot of the ideas were awesome, and subsequent game systems/settings have proved that it can totally work. It\u2019s definitely not the over the top gonzo nature of it that is inherently a problem. It\u2019s just that with the system and setting we already had it didn\u2019t work right. The mechanics for forging new worlds or remaking all of Creation don\u2019t mesh with a system originally designed to be over-the-top action by way of saying that rather than having to make a DC20 acrobatics check to fire a bow while doing a leaping backflip, you have to make a difficulty 0-1 roll and get a bonus to your accuracy instead. It\u2019s like trying to play MtG with Uno cards*<br /> <br /> The setting is also just cool in a lot of places, but it made a lot of 2e games feel like that\u2019s the goal, and also the super gonzo elders who are still around are playing that game of destruction of all creation being a speed bump. It\u2019s like starting a book off with a picture of a galaxy and saying \u201cthis image is not of space and stars, but the Wyld, and worlds. Each mote of light you see is a creation, with its own gods, primordials, hell and underworld. Now let me tell you about the beings who wave their hands and scatter thousands of these worlds, like dust, And of the heroes who fight them.\u201d That could be an amazing setting! But it\u2019s one that can really cheapen the rest of Creation, and puts an enormous temptation to suddenly upscale plots to the level of ubergods who throw around planes of existence like grains of sand.<br /> <br /> <br /> *or maybe more accurately trying to play Uno with MtG cards considering the styles of the various systems that work like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T10:55:08-07:00","id":1411834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1411754#post1411754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I get what you mean by a joke. It looks like it's written by Terry Pratchett explaining how the dwarves in \u00dcberwald handle trash, making a list of trash that dwarves produces &quot;used pickaxe, worthless rocks&quot; and adding a casual &quot;Troll brains&quot; to remind everyone that dwarves hates trolls and view them as lesser beings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Damn you people are no fucking fun. It takes <i>effort</i> to be this much of a negative bitch about a single funny line in a book.<br /> <br /> I am such a DB fanboy one of my own DB's learned CCS and ascended beyond being Terrestrial into being some strange Gaian Primordial Exalt and I still think it was funny.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1411793#post1411793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It\u2019s <i>very</i> amusing. Just, you know, in a way that <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1411754#post1411754\">Chausse already described best</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sorry no, I don't believe it. Please do not <i>speak</i> for my opinion on things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4801,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","user":"Frostav","date":". 09-04-2020, 01:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","name":"Frostav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T11:40:23-07:00","id":1411843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1411834#post1411834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Damn you people are no fucking fun. It takes <i>effort</i> to be this much of a negative bitch about a single funny line in a book.<br /> <br /> I am such a DB fanboy one of my own DB's learned CCS and ascended beyond being Terrestrial into being some strange Gaian Primordial Exalt and I still think it was funny.<br /> <br /> Sorry no, I don't believe it. Please do not <i>speak</i> for my opinion on things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I like this kind of joke, I find them funny. I just think there are different kind of interpretations. If you want to take the more light hearted interpretation and take it the more joke-y way it's up to you and that's cool, but I think this is also something that can show how Solars looks down on DB.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T14:23:06-07:00","id":1411883,"title":"","content":"In my opinion, the biggest mistake with Dreams of the First Age is it came out before something like Shards of the Exalted Dream.<br /> As such it was lapped up by people who wanted to play Exalted Modern or Exalted Space Adventures rather than engage with its premise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T14:40:19-07:00","id":1411890,"title":"","content":"I honestly never envisioned I AM being <i>a computer</i> as such. I AM is a person, who speaks out of objects like someone on the other end of a two-way speaker. A person with vast knowledge of almost every subject, perfect memory, and the ability to hold an absurd number of simultaneous conversations and relay information quickly between one conversation to another. He makes a great telephone, except a telephone conversation routed through I AM is going to be like those conversations on sitcoms where two people are mad at each other and not on speaking terms, but are each speaking through a friend who can still speak to both of them. &quot;Tell Hellen to pass the salt.&quot; &quot;Tell Peter he can reach for it himself.&quot;<br /> <br /> What he doesn't make is a good graphics card. There aren't I AM websites. There's just a voice that knows a ton of stuff, is good at doing math and reciting encyclopedia articles, and who knows everyone in the world like, at the very least, a familiar acquaintance and sometimes like a close friend.<br /> <br /> There's probably screens and a text interface only inasmuch as there would need to be to let him communicate with folks with hearing or speaking impairment.<br /> <br /> So, like, he's definitely social media! You can use him to keep up with what your friends are doing, as long as your friends are telling him what they're doing and have told him it's okay for him to relay that info to you. And he knows almost everyone so he can definitely introduce you to someone on the other side of Creation who you'd probably really like, or who has a shared interest, and then you could talk to them through him. But he's not <i>the Internet</i>. He's something that is being used in a very similar societal niche <i>as</i> the Internet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":229,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","user":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","date":". 09-04-2020, 05:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T14:43:21-07:00","id":1411892,"title":"","content":"I think also a bit that messed with things is Exalted's relationshipw ith Dreams and the subsequent linew, hcih also is why I see what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar229_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"229\" data-vbnamecard=\"229\">Stephen Lea Sheppard</a> was going for, but I think also probalby a bit the issue. Aberrant was a different genre than expected, but it didn't stop Aeon from like, being that still. And Adventure! didn't requir eyou know anyting about the other games (I actually read neither unitl the KSes but Adventure! is one of my favorit games of all time).<br /> <br /> Dreams had kind of what I call the Star Wars Prequel issue going on. Not only did it revela a lot, but it kind of back-flooded into future stuff that had it set down adn so drew on that. I noticed a lot of the setting books in some fashion drew lines back to DotFA material when they were less likely to before. ANd due to how mechanized a lot of it was, a lot of its achievements and presentation of the world became a thing folks thought htey had to build back towards, rather than something lost to the ages to make something else.<br /> <br /> I guess a way to think of it, it was more in the end like Vampire: the Dark Ages than Aberrant in relation to the first game. And since it was sold as a supplement for Exalted, not a new game in itself, I think tha talso warped a lot of how it was received. I think the setting presented has some things worth thinking on, but htey probablya s also noted work better as a Shard rather then a historical setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T17:04:53-07:00","id":1411943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1411834#post1411834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Damn you people are no fucking fun. It takes <i>effort</i> to be this much of a negative bitch about a single funny line in a book.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Leave the thread and take a warning.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T20:14:17-07:00","id":1411994,"title":"","content":"Seconding Blaque, the one time I checked out a 2e book every location featured had at least a page of \u201cWhat was this place like in the First Age\u201d as if it goes without saying that everyone is going to play a DotFA game at some point and desperately needs to know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T02:52:53-07:00","id":1412030,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar229_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"229\" data-vbnamecard=\"229\">Stephen Lea Sheppard</a> thank you. That helps a lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T07:06:51-07:00","id":1412073,"title":"","content":"Put that way, IAM sounds more like GPT3(+Siri+Google) than internet.<br /> <br /> (On a tangent, GPT3 and this discussion has made me think again about an old post of mine on here in where we discussed constructed intelligences in Exalted, where I thought that they owed a lot to the assumptions of early to mid 20th century sci-fi about what would be easy and hard - that matching basic sentience and sapience to a roughly human level would be easy, but exceeding it from then on would be hard. IAM has a little of that quality perhaps, in that it is a little reminiscent of something like Ship's Computer in '60s Star Trek or HAL 9000, which could easy vocally interact with the crew, but their vid interfaces were pretty primitive. In the same spirit, GPT3 seems to offer some indications that, where we thought that coding AI to generate new expertise might be easy, but new creative output would be hard, it seems that there are some indications that it's the opposite. It seems relatively easy to prompt GPT3 to generate, for instance, new Cowboy Bebop episode plot outlines - if ones you'd probably reject as a series planner! - or Neil Gaiman parody... but hard to get it to develop any novel unguided expertise that isn't just a reprint of a text that it's effectively found through search.)<br /> <br /> On another point I'm a bit surprised that Exalted's First Age development ever considered Exalted Modern as an option - the Records of the Before and all the developer commentary was pointing to them having mecha, sky carriers, automata, and generally stuff that was beyond late 20th century (&quot;modern&quot;), or if beyond per se, not exactly the same. Or maybe I'm not getting what Exalted Modern means in that context!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T07:17:56-07:00","id":1412078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1411890#post1411890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What he doesn't make is a good graphics card. There aren't I AM websites. There's just a voice that knows a ton of stuff, is good at doing math and reciting encyclopedia articles, and who knows everyone in the world like, at the very least, a familiar acquaintance and sometimes like a close friend.<br /> <br /> There's probably screens and a text interface only inasmuch as there would need to be to let him communicate with folks with hearing or speaking impairment.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe a reference to things like opera performances being broadcast via I AM managed to sneak in there.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T15:19:08-07:00","id":1412171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1411750#post1411750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, funfact: I pitched for a writing job on Dreams of the First Age not because I thought I had any good ideas, or even because I was excited by the prospect of working on it, but because back then I was still committed to collecting every Exalted book and thought it'd be easier to get ahold of this one if I wrote for it and got a comp copy than if I had to buy it.</div> </div> </div> </div> This is the only just and true reason to write.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T19:41:07-07:00","id":1412203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1411749#post1411749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In retrospect none of this was a good idea because . . . I'm not Jewish so doing anything with any variation of I AM THAT I AM is probably insensitive. Especially writing Him as a cross between the Internet and Gamera. . . .<br /> <br /> I hope this post helps to contextualize my previous comment, &quot;Hoo boy, am I conflicted.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It was insensitive to Christians too, but speaking as one I still thought it was a decent what-if and very much in line with Aquinas' ideas on why the Greek works were worth studying by people who didn't share the faith. It chapped me briefly, but I realized the problem was in my reaction not being very Grace-filled (like, same day realization). (Put another way, something can be insensitive without being offensive if the audience is willing to listen.)<br /> <br /> So... keep being conflicted, in the best possible way I guess? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13194-psyclus","name":"Psyclus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-06T10:03:41-07:00","id":1412306,"title":"","content":"Oh right something else that really disappointing about Dreams of the First Age. <br /> <br /> Compass: Scavenger Lands made Shield of a Different Day the goddess of a lost concept of 'peaceful warfare' its glaringly absent given how much this setting seems to be about how First Age Solars keep score among themselves without ending up with a repeat of the Thousand Struggles Era. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-09T22:08:42-07:00","id":1412797,"title":"","content":"One thing talked about on RPG.net was about how in some respects the &quot;Dreams&quot; of the first age fell sort of flat for us, because many of the attributes would have been familiar to anyone living in a modern nation. (Vacations, abundant food, medical care, etc. ). Someone, I forget who, mentioned that it sounded like, absent the presence of the supernatural, a bit like living in Western Europe.<br /> <br /> And I think one of the issues is the dissonance between us-as-people and characters in the setting.<br /> <br /> Because for any character, in the &quot;present&quot; era of Exalted, that very much <i>would</i> have been a dream, hard infact for them to even conceive of. But again, for us, typing on a computer in our air-conditioned room, it was a bit more familiar. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-10T04:12:44-07:00","id":1412828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NewK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1412797#post1412797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing talked about on RPG.net was about how in some respects the &quot;Dreams&quot; of the first age fell sort of flat for us, because many of the attributes would have been familiar to anyone living in a modern nation. (Vacations, abundant food, medical care, etc. ). Someone, I forget who, mentioned that it sounded like, absent the presence of the supernatural, a bit like living in Western Europe.<br /> <br /> And I think one of the issues is the dissonance between us-as-people and characters in the setting.<br /> <br /> Because for any character, in the &quot;present&quot; era of Exalted, that very much <i>would</i> have been a dream, hard infact for them to even conceive of. But again, for us, typing on a computer in our air-conditioned room, it was a bit more familiar. <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s exactly what I liked about it. The contrast between the First and Second Ages. And I guess the Shogunate (which always makes me think of Kamakura Era Japan, like in the Tale of the Heike). (I took a class on Japanese history in school.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-10T08:51:17-07:00","id":1412854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1412828#post1412828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That\u2019s exactly what I liked about it. The contrast between the First and Second Ages. And I guess the Shogunate (which always makes me think of Kamakura Era Japan, like in the Tale of the Heike). (I took a class on Japanese history in school.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think though it plays a bit on what SLS noted. There's an expectation of waht the FA is, it was actually basiclaly early 21st Century Earth running on Makotech, and while that's a nice subversion in a literay sense, it is not very engaging or interesting in a context of Exalted and actively feels like it's trying to deconstruct for its own sake rather than provide something to stimulate an intersting game.<br /> <br /> Like, for me at lest, on the timeline I thought the Ochre Fountian was striclty more interesting a time period than anything invovling the hgihg First Age, and that's simply due to how broad it felt and <i>not</i> settled into a routine it seemed like then, as well as having at least a lot more &quot;new to the world&quot; like broken Dragon Kings, still Jadeborn and Autochthon around and no one world government.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-10T09:02:59-07:00","id":1412855,"title":"","content":"Considering how utterly differently the history of the Exalted setting <b>must be</b> from our world, it feels pretty egocentric to write it so that <i>a world that looks like ours</i> is what happens when you have a bunch of awesome people steering the development of human civilization.<br /> <br /> \u200bI can't find the posts now, but I liked some of the speculation Isator Levi did about the First Age.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-10T12:01:19-07:00","id":1412873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1412854#post1412854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think though it plays a bit on what SLS noted. There's an expectation of waht the FA is, it was actually basiclaly early 21st Century Earth running on Makotech, and while that's a nice subversion in a literay sense, it is not very engaging or interesting in a context of Exalted and actively feels like it's trying to deconstruct for its own sake rather than provide something to stimulate an intersting game.<br /> <br /> Like, for me at lest, on the timeline I thought the Ochre Fountian was striclty more interesting a time period than anything invovling the hgihg First Age, and that's simply due to how broad it felt and <i>not</i> settled into a routine it seemed like then, as well as having at least a lot more &amp;quot;new to the world&amp;quot; like broken Dragon Kings, still Jadeborn and Autochthon around and no one world government.</div> </div> </div> </div>What did you think of the Modern Age shard from Shards of the Exalted Dream? I liked it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-10T13:38:43-07:00","id":1412890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1412873#post1412873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What did you think of the Modern Age shard from Shards of the Exalted Dream? I liked it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's alright but probably in the mush of &quot;Not Heaven's Reach&quot; for me, so there's that. And noteably even though it's neat, it's not the defnitive history of the world. It is like what was stated earlier. Dreams would have made for a pretty good shard. As the default-assumed actual history of the setting, it has a lot of issues, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-10T13:41:55-07:00","id":1412891,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1458\" data-vbnamecard=\"1458\">NewK</a>, subjectively I have the impression that in the noughts, at the time, there was a lot of zeigeisty enthusiasm on Rpg.net for settings which talked about how the inevitable consequences of frequent, available, accessible, reliable magic were some form of modernization or even &quot;more advanced than modern&quot; society (up to and including &quot;magical singularity&quot;).<br /> <br /> (Which idea Exalted perhaps was influential on, as I do think it was deeply influential on RPG settings in the noughts!).<br /> <br /> I think this has sort of started to wane a bit by the time DotFA came out, unfortunately for it, so that it was doing something which became out of fashion. I can't really speculate as to why this is; it could be because of a resurgence of enthusiasm for old fashioned fantasy settings with lots of magic which were not modern or &quot;advanced&quot; or because of some changing emphasis on importance of political structures to modern society above technology and growth (perhaps a move in the wrong direction I would hazard a guess). There are still some settings working in this space of &quot;Magic -&gt; Advanced Society&quot; like Colin Fredericks's &quot;Sorcerously Advanced&quot; though. I do think stuff like &quot;Sorcerously Advanced&quot; (which is pretty cool) benefits from not having to serve as frame narrative for something else, as the First Age must. (RPG.net itself of course has been through many permutations of what is fashionable to talk about since DotFA!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-10T17:34:05-07:00","id":1412933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1412891#post1412891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1458\" data-vbnamecard=\"1458\">NewK</a>, subjectively I have the impression that in the noughts, at the time, there was a lot of zeigeisty enthusiasm on Rpg.net for settings which talked about how the inevitable consequences of frequent, available, accessible, reliable magic were some form of modernization or even &quot;more advanced than modern&quot; society (up to and including &quot;magical singularity&quot;).<br /> <br /> (Which idea Exalted perhaps was influential on, as I do think it was deeply influential on RPG settings in the noughts!).<br /> <br /> I think this has sort of started to wane a bit by the time DotFA came out, unfortunately for it, so that it was doing something which became out of fashion. I can't really speculate as to why this is; it could be because of a resurgence of enthusiasm for old fashioned fantasy settings with lots of magic which were not modern or &quot;advanced&quot; or because of some changing emphasis on importance of political structures to modern society above technology and growth (perhaps a move in the wrong direction I would hazard a guess). There are still some settings working in this space of &quot;Magic -&gt; Advanced Society&quot; like Colin Fredericks's &quot;Sorcerously Advanced&quot; though. I do think stuff like &quot;Sorcerously Advanced&quot; (which is pretty cool) benefits from not having to serve as frame narrative for something else, as the First Age must. (RPG.net itself of course has been through many permutations of what is fashionable to talk about since DotFA!)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That was the Tippyverse era wasn't it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-10T17:52:24-07:00","id":1412935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NewK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1412797#post1412797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">many of the attributes would have been familiar to anyone living in a modern nation. (Vacations, abundant food, medical care, etc. ).</div> </div> </div> </div>When you say familiar do you mean personal experience or awareness of it as a thing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-11T00:09:51-07:00","id":1412967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1412935#post1412935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When you say familiar do you mean personal experience or awareness of it as a thing?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think that the personal experience thing is irrelevant because he's describing the (ideal) functioning of a social model which is in place in Western Europe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":24291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","user":"Chausse","date":". 09-11-2020, 05:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-14T05:36:23-07:00","id":1413541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1412873#post1412873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What did you think of the Modern Age shard from Shards of the Exalted Dream? I liked it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shards made me appreciate how badly DotFA utilised the space that it had available to it. Like there's huge holes in what we know about the 3 settings due to word count limitations but Dreams doesn't really have anymore depth for having two books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-15T18:52:04-07:00","id":1413883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1413541#post1413541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shards made me appreciate how badly DotFA utilised the space that it had available to it. Like there's huge holes in what we know about the 3 settings due to word count limitations but Dreams doesn't really have anymore depth for having two books.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If it was possible to bind and loose and go back and have it redone, I'd just tell them: Cut out the stat blocks of the NPCs, save maybe for a few biggies, like what their finishing move is, and maybe what tehy're supposedly really good at, because most of th eNPCs as I remember were pretty much: &quot;Every printed charm: yes.&quot; <br /> <br /> And I think that was another problem--Exalted is fluffed as &quot;Waht would you do with the power of a demigod&quot; and unfortunately, DOFTA, even if you took the semi-experienced exalt option, often boiled that down to: Do whatever your far more awesome elders told you to.<br /> <br /> It's funny, but I think one thing that would drastically help DOFTA is the current dynamic in 3E, where Essence 6 plus may get you some weird and useful charms, but nothing really <i>more</i> powerful, not drastically so, than what anyone can get at essence 5. It would have allowed the setting to show how &quot;quirky&quot; exalts could get, via the special charms they'd developed, while avoiding the problem of &quot;wow, these guys can curbstomp us by rolling over in their sleep.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-16T10:24:33-07:00","id":1413987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409323-what-do-you-guys-think-of-dreams-of-the-first-age?p=1412933#post1412933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was the Tippyverse era wasn't it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, blast from the past there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}